owser unresponsive. We recommend files under 5 million faces.\"}},\"Button\":{\"Cancel\":\"Cancel\"},\"Heading\":{\"Default\":\"Drag and drop file here or click to upload\",\"Dragging\":\"Drop file here\",\"Uploaded\":\"Model uploaded\",\"Uploading\":\"Uploading...\"},\"Message\":{\"FormatError\":\"Please upload a supported file format\",\"NumberError\":\"Please upload a single file\",\"SizeError\":\"Please upload a file smaller than 100 MB\",\"SizeWarning\":\"Please note that uploading large 3D model files (\u003e50 MB) may reduce performance of the 3D viewport or make the browser unresponsive. We recommend uploading files with no more than 5 million faces in total.\"}},\"Pagination\":{\"Current\":\"\u003cb\u003e{current}\u003c/b\u003e of {total}\",\"CurrentPage\":{\"LastPart\":\" of {total}\"},\"RecordsPerPage\":\"Records per page\"},\"Search\":{\"Empty\":\"No results found.\",\"Placeholder\":{\"Community\":\"Search model / user\",\"General\":\"Search\",\"Generation\":\"Search my generation\"},\"Reset\":\"Clear\"},\"SliderInput\":{\"ErrorOutOfRange\":\"Please enter a number between {min} and {max}.\"},\"StatusTag\":{\"Canceled\":\"Canceled\",\"Failed\":\"Failed\",\"FailedGenerating\":\"Generating failed\",\"FailedRemeshing\":\"Remeshing failed\",\"FailedRigging\":\"Rigging failed\",\"FailedStylizing\":\"Stylizing failed\",\"FailedTexturing\":\"Texturing failed\",\"Finished\":\"Finished\",\"Generating\":\"Generating\",\"Preparing\":\"Creating ...\",\"Queuing\":\"Queuing\",\"Remeshing\":\"Remeshing\",\"Rigging\":\"Rigging\",\"Stylizing\":\"Stylizing\",\"Texturing\":\"Texturing\"},\"Table\":{\"NoData\":\"No data\"},\"TargetPolycount\":{\"WarningOutOfRange\":\"Reducing the number of polygons to lower than {n} may result in significant quality loss.\"},\"Time\":{\"Added\":\"Added\",\"Created\":\"Created\",\"CreatedAt\":\"Created At\"},\"Viewer\":{\"AnimationPlaceholder\":\"Please select an action from the animation library.\",\"Error\":{\"CopyErrorDetail\":\"Copy Error Details\",\"Default\":\"Model loading failed.\",\"ErrorCreatingWebGLContext\":\"Unable to initiate 3D model viewer. Try updating your browser or graphics card driver to the latest version.\",\"Retry\":\"Retry\"},\"Placeholder\":\"Choose a model to edit\"}},\"Components\":{\"Community\":{\"CreatorCard\":{\"FollowersCount\":\"{count} Followers\",\"FollowingsCount\":\"{count} Followings\"},\"Discover\":{\"CreatePrompt\":\"What will you create in 3D?\",\"Greeting\":\"Hi, {nickname}!\"},\"SpotlightCard\":{\"DownloadModel\":\"Download model\",\"SendTip\":\"Send a tip\",\"ShareModel\":\"Share model\",\"ViewComments\":\"View comments\"}},\"Discover\":{\"AgentMode\":\"Agent Mode\",\"AgentPlaceholder\":\"Describe your idea and start creating with Agent\",\"NewBadge\":\"New\",\"QuickGenerate\":\"Quick Generate\",\"QuickGenerateFromImage\":\"Quick Generate from an Image\",\"QuickStart\":\"Quick start\",\"UploadImage\":\"Upload image\"},\"EventTag\":{\"Or\":\"or\",\"StageEnds\":\"Stage ends:\",\"TwoWaysToJoin\":\"Two Ways to Join\"},\"IdleEngagement\":{\"CarouselNav\":{\"Close\":\"Close\",\"Next\":\"Next\",\"Previous\":\"Previous\"},\"Reaction\":{\"AddToCollection\":\"Add to collection\",\"Heart\":\"Heart\",\"ROFL\":\"Laugh\",\"Smile\":\"Smile\",\"ThumbUp\":\"Thumbs up\"}},\"ImageUploadArea\":{\"MaxSize\":\"Max size: {maxSize}MB\",\"ReUpload\":\"Re-Upload\",\"Supported\":\"Supported Formats: {accept}\",\"Title\":\"Click \u003ci\u003e/\u003c/i\u003e Drag \u0026 Drop \u003ci\u003e/\u003c/i\u003e Paste Image\",\"Uploading\":\"Uploading ...\"},\"Integrations\":{\"AgentSection\":{\"Block\":{\"Copied\":\"Copied\",\"Copy\":\"Copy\",\"Terminal\":\"Terminal\",\"WorksWith\":\"Works with\"},\"Description\":\"Connect Meshy to any AI coding assistant through the MCP protocol or Skills — describe what you need and let the agent handle the rest.\",\"Heading\":\"Let AI agents create 3D for you\",\"MCP\":{\"Description\":\"Install the Meshy MCP Server to bring AI-powered 3D generation into any MCP-compatible client.\",\"Title\":\"MCP Server\"},\"SectionLabel\":\"Agent Integrations\",\"Skills\":{\"Description\":\"Add Meshy 3D generation as a skill for your AI coding assistant — works with any IDE that supports npx skills.\",\"Title\":\"Skills\"}},\"Badge\":{\"Native\":\"Native\",\"OneClick\":\"One-Click\",\"Plugin\":\"Plugin\"},\"Card\":{\"BambuStudio\":\"Send to Bambu Studio directly from your workspace — no plugin needed.\",\"Blender\":\"Bridge AI models into Blender — plus built-in analysis, cleanup, and export tools.\",\"ComfyUI\":\"Generate 3D models inside ComfyUI workflows — native Partner Node, no plugin install.\",\"CrealityPrint\":\"Send to Creality Print directly from your workspace — no plugin needed.\",\"ElegooSlicer\":\"Send to Elegoo Slicer directly from your workspace — no plugin needed.\",\"FlashStudio\":\"Send to Flash Studio directly from your workspace — no plugin needed.\",\"Godot\":\"Bridge game-ready assets into Godot — meshes, PBR textures, and animations.\",\"LycheeSlicer\":\"Send to Lychee Slicer directly from your workspace — no plugin needed.\",\"Maya\":\"Bridge AI models into Maya — import, edit, and render without manual downloads.\",\"Omniverse\":\"Send Meshy models into Omniverse or Isaac Sim with Sim-Ready physics, collision, and semantic labels.\",\"OrcaSlicer\":\"Send to OrcaSlicer directly from your workspace — no plugin needed.\",\"RobloxStudio\":\"Upload AI models to Roblox Creator Hub as GLB assets via the Meshy Bridge app.\",\"SnapmakerOrca\":\"Send to Snapmaker Orca directly from your workspace — no plugin needed.\",\"ThreeDsMax\":\"Bridge AI models into 3ds Max — import, edit, and render without manual downloads.\",\"UltimakerCura\":\"Send to Ultimaker Cura directly from your workspace — no plugin needed.\",\"Unity\":\"Bridge game-ready assets into Unity — meshes, PBR textures, and animations.\",\"UnrealEngine\":\"Bridge game-ready assets into Unreal Engine — meshes, PBR textures, and animations.\",\"ZBrush\":\"Bridge AI models into ZBrush — import clean OBJ geometry straight onto the canvas to sculpt.\"},\"Categories\":{\"AIAgents\":\"AI Agents\",\"API\":\"API\",\"GameEngine\":\"Game Engine\",\"GameEngines\":\"Game Engines\",\"PhysicsSimulation\":\"Physics Simulation\",\"ThreeDModeling\":\"3D Modeling\",\"ThreeDPrinting\":\"3D Printing\"},\"CategoryNav\":{\"All\":\"All\"},\"Detail\":{\"AllIntegrations\":\"All Integrations\",\"BackToAll\":\"Back to all integrations\",\"CTAButton\":\"Start for Free\",\"CTATitle\":\"Install in minutes.\",\"ComingSoon\":\"Detailed documentation for this integration is coming soon.\",\"Documentation\":\"Documentation\",\"DownloadPlugin\":\"Download Plugin\",\"FAQ\":\"Frequently Asked Questions\",\"Features\":\"Features\",\"GettingStarted\":\"Getting Started\",\"MeshyFor\":\"Meshy for {name}\",\"Overview\":\"Overview\",\"QuickFacts\":\"Quick Facts\",\"Requirements\":\"Requirements\",\"SelectPlatform\":\"Choose your platform\",\"SelectVersion\":\"Choose a version\",\"ViewDocumentation\":\"View Documentation\",\"Website\":\"{name} Website\"},\"Details\":{\"BambuStudio\":{\"features\":{\"0\":{\"bullets\":{\"0\":\"Click Print → Send to Bambu Studio from any model in your workspace\",\"1\":\"Model automatically downloads and opens in Bambu Studio\",\"2\":\"Works with all Meshy-generated models and community models\",\"3\":\"No manual file downloading or importing required\"},\"description\":\"Send models from your Meshy workspace directly to Bambu Studio with a single click via the Print menu.\",\"title\":\"One-Click Print Workflow\"},\"1\":{\"bullets\":{\"0\":\"Automatic application launch with model pre-loaded\",\"1\":\"Confirm the prompt to allow the transfer\",\"2\":\"Supports all model types generated by Meshy\"},\"description\":\"The integration uses protocol linking to open Bambu Studio automatically with your model loaded.\",\"title\":\"Seamless Integration\"}},\"headline\":\"Send AI-generated 3D models directly to Bambu Studio for one-click 3D printing.\",\"installSteps\":{\"0\":\"Open a model in your Meshy workspace.\",\"1\":\"Click the Print menu and select Send to Bambu Studio.\",\"2\":\"Confirm the browser prompt to open Bambu Studio.\",\"3\":\"The model loads automatically — slice and print.\"},\"overview\":\"Meshy integrates with Bambu Studio — the official slicer for Bambu Lab 3D printers — so you can go from AI generation to print-ready slicing in seconds. Select any model in your Meshy workspace, hit Print, and it opens automatically in Bambu Studio ready to slice.\",\"requirements\":{\"0\":\"Bambu Studio installed on your computer\",\"1\":\"A Meshy Pro account or above\"}},\"Blender\":{\"faqs\":{\"0\":{\"a\":\"Yes, free to download. A Meshy Pro account or above is required to use the DCC Bridge.\",\"q\":\"Is the Meshy Blender plugin free?\"},\"1\":{\"a\":\"Blender 4.2.6 or later is required. We recommend staying on the latest stable Blender release for best compatibility.\",\"q\":\"Which Blender versions are supported?\"},\"2\":{\"a\":\"Yes. Model generation and Bridge transfers both require an active internet connection to communicate with Meshy's cloud services.\",\"q\":\"Do I need an internet connection to use the plugin?\"},\"3\":{\"a\":\"The Bridge transfers models in GLB (recommended — textures embedded) or ZIP (separate texture files). GLB works best for most Blender workflows.\",\"q\":\"What file formats does the Bridge transfer?\"},\"4\":{\"a\":\"Linux is not officially supported. The plugin is tested on macOS and Windows only.\",\"q\":\"Does the plugin work on Linux?\"}},\"features\":{\"0\":{\"bullets\":{\"0\":\"One-click import from MeshyAI workspace\",\"1\":\"Automatic format detection and import (GLB, ZIP)\",\"2\":\"Preserves materials, textures, and color attributes\",\"3\":\"Works with any model in your workspace or the community gallery\"},\"description\":\"One-click model transfer from the MeshyAI webapp to Blender via a local HTTP bridge. Supports GLB and ZIP formats with automatic optimization.\",\"title\":\"Bridge to Blender\"},\"1\":{\"bullets\":{\"0\":\"Volume and surface area calculations\",\"1\":\"Solid/watertight verification\",\"2\":\"Self-intersection detection\",\"3\":\"Thickness, overhang, and sharp edge analysis\",\"4\":\"Small pieces detection\"},\"description\":\"Comprehensive geometry checking tools designed for 3D printing preparation. Run all checks at once or inspect individual properties.\",\"title\":\"Model Analysis\"},\"2\":{\"bullets\":{\"0\":\"Make Manifold — fix non-manifold geometry, fill holes, merge duplicate vertices\",\"1\":\"Delete Small Pieces — remove fragments by volume, area, or diagonal\",\"2\":\"Automatic normal direction correction\"},\"description\":\"Automated repair tools to fix common geometry problems and make models print-ready.\",\"title\":\"Model Cleanup\"},\"3\":{\"bullets\":{\"0\":\"Hollow — create offset surfaces for hollow prints\",\"1\":\"Align XY — orient models flat on the print bed\",\"2\":\"Scale to Volume and Scale to Bounds\"},\"description\":\"Preparation tools to modify and orient models for optimal printing results.\",\"title\":\"Model Editing\"},\"4\":{\"bullets\":{\"0\":\"STL export for 3D printing\",\"1\":\"OBJ export for general 3D modeling\",\"2\":\"PLY export with vertex colors\",\"3\":\"Configurable export options (UVs, normals, textures)\"},\"description\":\"Export cleaned and prepared models in multiple formats for 3D printing and sharing.\",\"title\":\"Model Export\"}},\"headline\":\"Generate and import AI 3D models directly inside Blender with the official Meshy plugin.\",\"howToHeading\":\"How to install \u0026 use Meshy for Blender\",\"installSteps\":{\"0\":\"Download the plugin ZIP from this page (or via Resources in the Meshy navigation). Do not unzip—Blender installs directly from the ZIP file.\",\"1\":\"In Blender, open Edit → Preferences → Add-ons, click the arrow in the top right, and select Install from Disk.\",\"2\":\"Select the downloaded ZIP file — or drag and drop it into the Blender viewport.\",\"3\":\"Open the Meshy panel in the viewport sidebar (press N). Paste your Meshy API key to activate the Bridge feature.\"},\"overview\":\"Meshy for Blender is a free plugin that connects MeshyAI's 3D generation to your Blender workspace. Transfer AI-generated models with one click via the DCC Bridge — no downloading or manual importing. The plugin also includes a full suite of 3D-print preparation tools: geometry analysis, automated cleanup, model editing, and multi-format export.\",\"quickFacts\":{\"0\":{\"label\":\"Type\",\"value\":\"Official Blender add-on (ZIP)\"},\"1\":{\"label\":\"Blender version\",\"value\":\"4.2.6+\"},\"2\":{\"label\":\"Account\",\"value\":\"Meshy Pro or above\"},\"3\":{\"label\":\"Bridge\",\"value\":\"Requires Meshy API key\"},\"4\":{\"label\":\"Formats\",\"value\":\"GLB, ZIP\"},\"5\":{\"label\":\"Best for\",\"value\":\"DCC iteration + 3D print prep\"}},\"requirements\":{\"0\":\"Blender 4.2.6 or later\",\"1\":\"A Meshy Pro account or above\",\"2\":\"Meshy API key (for Bridge feature)\"}},\"CrealityPrint\":{\"features\":{\"0\":{\"bullets\":{\"0\":\"Click Print → Send to Creality Print from any model in your workspace\",\"1\":\"Model automatically downloads and opens in Creality Print\",\"2\":\"Works with all Meshy-generated models and community models\",\"3\":\"No manual file downloading or importing required\"},\"description\":\"Send models from your Meshy workspace directly to Creality Print via the Print menu.\",\"title\":\"One-Click Print Workflow\"},\"1\":{\"bullets\":{\"0\":\"Native support for all Creality printer models\",\"1\":\"Pre-configured printer profiles for quick setup\",\"2\":\"macOS note: launch Creality Print before sending to avoid refresh issues\"},\"description\":\"Optimized for Creality's full range of FDM and resin printers.\",\"title\":\"Creality Ecosystem\"}},\"headline\":\"Send AI-generated 3D models directly to Creality Print for seamless printing on Creality printers.\",\"installSteps\":{\"0\":\"Open a model in your Meshy workspace.\",\"1\":\"Click the Print menu and select Send to Creality Print.\",\"2\":\"Confirm the browser prompt to open Creality Print.\",\"3\":\"The model loads automatically — slice and print.\"},\"overview\":\"Meshy integrates with Creality Print — the official slicer for Creality 3D printers. Transfer models from your Meshy workspace with one click. On macOS, launch Creality Print before sending to avoid a known refresh issue.\",\"requirements\":{\"0\":\"Creality Print installed on your computer\",\"1\":\"A Meshy Pro account or above\"}},\"ElegooSlicer\":{\"features\":{\"0\":{\"bullets\":{\"0\":\"Click Print → Send to Elegoo Slicer from any model in your workspace\",\"1\":\"Model automatically downloads and opens in Elegoo Slicer\",\"2\":\"Select the imported model in the Elegoo Slicer interface to begin\",\"3\":\"Works with all Meshy-generated models and community models\"},\"description\":\"Send models from your Meshy workspace directly to Elegoo Slicer via the Print menu.\",\"title\":\"One-Click Print Workflow\"},\"1\":{\"bullets\":{\"0\":\"Optimized for Elegoo's full range of printers\",\"1\":\"Supports both resin and FDM slicing profiles\",\"2\":\"Detailed support generation for resin prints\"},\"description\":\"Elegoo Slicer supports both resin (LCD/MSLA) and FDM printing workflows.\",\"title\":\"Resin \u0026 FDM Support\"}},\"headline\":\"Send AI-generated 3D models directly to Elegoo Slicer for resin printing preparation.\",\"installSteps\":{\"0\":\"Open a model in your Meshy workspace.\",\"1\":\"Click the Print menu and select Send to Elegoo Slicer.\",\"2\":\"Confirm the browser prompt to open Elegoo Slicer.\",\"3\":\"Select the imported model in the interface — slice and print.\"},\"overview\":\"Meshy integrates with Elegoo Slicer — the official slicer for Elegoo resin and FDM printers. Send models from your workspace with one click and start slicing immediately.\",\"requirements\":{\"0\":\"Elegoo Slicer installed on your computer\",\"1\":\"A Meshy Pro account or above\"}},\"FlashStudio\":{\"features\":{\"0\":{\"bullets\":{\"0\":\"Click Print → Send to Flash Studio from any model in your workspace\",\"1\":\"Model automatically downloads and opens in Flash Studio\",\"2\":\"Works with all Meshy-generated models and community models\",\"3\":\"No manual file downloading or importing required\"},\"description\":\"Send models from your Meshy workspace directly to Flash Studio with a single click via the Print menu.\",\"title\":\"One-Click Print Workflow\"},\"1\":{\"bullets\":{\"0\":\"Native support for Flashforge printer models\",\"1\":\"Pre-configured printer profiles for quick setup\",\"2\":\"Confirm the prompt to allow the transfer\"},\"description\":\"Optimized for Flashforge's full range of FDM 3D printers.\",\"title\":\"Flashforge Ecosystem\"}},\"headline\":\"Send AI-generated 3D models directly to Flash Studio for one-click 3D printing on Flashforge printers.\",\"installSteps\":{\"0\":\"Open a model in your Meshy workspace.\",\"1\":\"Click the Print menu and select Send to Flash Studio.\",\"2\":\"Confirm the browser prompt to open Flash Studio.\",\"3\":\"The model loads automatically — slice and print.\"},\"overview\":\"Meshy integrates with Flash Studio — the official slicer for Flashforge 3D printers — so you can go from AI generation to print-ready slicing in seconds. Select any model in your Meshy workspace, hit Print, and it opens automatically in Flash Studio ready to slice.\",\"requirements\":{\"0\":\"Flash Studio installed on your computer\",\"1\":\"A Meshy Pro account or above\"}},\"Godot\":{\"faqs\":{\"0\":{\"a\":\"Yes, free to download. A Meshy Pro account or above is required to use the DCC Bridge.\",\"q\":\"Is the Meshy Godot plugin free?\"},\"1\":{\"a\":\"Unzip the plugin and place the folder inside the addons/ directory in your Godot project. Then enable it in Project Settings → Plugins.\",\"q\":\"Where do I put the plugin files?\"},\"2\":{\"a\":\"The most common cause is a missing main scene. Set your main scene in Project Settings before importing. Importing without it set will cause errors.\",\"q\":\"Why does importing fail?\"},\"3\":{\"a\":\"Yes. Animated models are fully supported.\",\"q\":\"Does it support animated models?\"},\"4\":{\"a\":\"Please refer to the Requirements section on this page for the confirmed minimum version.\",\"q\":\"Which Godot version is required?\"}},\"features\":{\"0\":{\"bullets\":{\"0\":\"Send models directly from your Meshy workspace to Godot\",\"1\":\"Automatic model download and import into your scene\",\"2\":\"Works with any model in your workspace or the community gallery\",\"3\":\"No manual file downloading or importing required\"},\"description\":\"One-click model transfer from the MeshyAI webapp to Godot via the DCC Bridge.\",\"title\":\"Bridge to Godot\"},\"1\":{\"bullets\":{\"0\":\"Full animation data preserved on import\",\"1\":\"Animation playback via the play button\",\"2\":\"Supports all Meshy animation types\"},\"description\":\"Import animated models with full animation data preservation.\",\"title\":\"Animated Model Support\"}},\"headline\":\"Import AI-generated 3D models directly into Godot Engine with the official Meshy plugin.\",\"howToHeading\":\"How to install \u0026 use Meshy for Godot\",\"installSteps\":{\"0\":\"Go to Resources in the MeshyAI website navigation and download the Godot plugin.\",\"1\":\"Create an addons folder in your project's FileSystem if it doesn't exist.\",\"2\":\"Unzip the plugin and drag the folder into the addons directory.\",\"3\":\"Open Project Settings → Plugins tab and enable the Meshy plugin. Set your main scene first—importing without it may cause errors. Send a model from Meshy to verify.\"},\"overview\":\"Meshy for Godot is a free plugin that brings one-click model import to the Godot Editor. Transfer models from your Meshy workspace via the DCC Bridge, with full support for animated models. Set your main scene before importing.\",\"quickFacts\":{\"0\":{\"label\":\"Type\",\"value\":\"Godot plugin (addons folder)\"},\"1\":{\"label\":\"Animated models\",\"value\":\"Supported\"},\"2\":{\"label\":\"Key requirement\",\"value\":\"Main scene must be set before importing\"}},\"requirements\":{\"0\":\"Godot Engine\",\"1\":\"A Meshy Pro account or above\",\"2\":\"Main scene must be set before importing\"}},\"LycheeSlicer\":{\"features\":{\"0\":{\"bullets\":{\"0\":\"Click Print → Send to Lychee Slicer from any model in your workspace\",\"1\":\"Enter a filename with .3mf extension when prompted\",\"2\":\"Model imports into Lychee Slicer for professional slicing\",\"3\":\"Works with all Meshy-generated models and community models\"},\"description\":\"Send models from your Meshy workspace directly to Lychee Slicer via the Print menu.\",\"title\":\"One-Click Print Workflow\"},\"1\":{\"bullets\":{\"0\":\"Supports a wide range of resin and FDM printers\",\"1\":\"Advanced automatic support generation\",\"2\":\"Professional print preparation workflow\",\"3\":\"Important: add .3mf extension when saving or the model will not load\"},\"description\":\"Lychee Slicer offers advanced features for high-quality resin and FDM printing.\",\"title\":\"Professional Slicing Tools\"}},\"headline\":\"Send AI-generated 3D models to Lychee Slicer for professional-grade resin print preparation.\",\"installSteps\":{\"0\":\"Open a model in your Meshy workspace.\",\"1\":\"Click the Print menu and select Send to Lychee Slicer.\",\"2\":\"Confirm the browser prompt and enter a filename with .3mf extension.\",\"3\":\"The model imports into Lychee Slicer — slice and print.\"},\"overview\":\"Meshy integrates with Lychee Slicer by Mango3D — a professional slicer supporting various 3D printer types. Important: when saving the model file, you must add the .3mf extension manually, or the model will fail to load.\",\"requirements\":{\"0\":\"Lychee Slicer installed on your computer\",\"1\":\"A Meshy Pro account or above\"}},\"Maya\":{\"faqs\":{\"0\":{\"a\":\"Yes, free to download. A Meshy Pro account or above is required to use the DCC Bridge.\",\"q\":\"Is the Meshy Maya plugin free?\"},\"1\":{\"a\":\"Open Maya's Plug-in Manager (Windows → Settings/Preferences → Plug-in Manager), click Browse, navigate to the plugin file, and enable it.\",\"q\":\"How do I load the plugin in Maya?\"},\"2\":{\"a\":\"Make sure your main scene is set before importing. Importing without a main scene may cause errors or unexpected behavior.\",\"q\":\"Why does importing fail?\"},\"3\":{\"a\":\"Yes. Animated models are fully supported.\",\"q\":\"Does it support animated models?\"},\"4\":{\"a\":\"Please refer to the Requirements section on this page for the confirmed minimum version.\",\"q\":\"Which Maya version is required?\"}},\"features\":{\"0\":{\"bullets\":{\"0\":\"Send models directly from your Meshy workspace to Maya\",\"1\":\"Automatic model download and import\",\"2\":\"Works with any model in your workspace or the community gallery\",\"3\":\"No manual file downloading or importing required\"},\"description\":\"One-click model transfer from the MeshyAI webapp to Maya via the DCC Bridge.\",\"title\":\"Bridge to Maya\"},\"1\":{\"bullets\":{\"0\":\"Full animation data preserved on import\",\"1\":\"Animation playback via slider control\",\"2\":\"Supports all Meshy animation types\"},\"description\":\"Import animated models with full animation data preservation.\",\"title\":\"Animated Model Support\"}},\"headline\":\"Import AI-generated 3D models directly into Autodesk Maya with the official Meshy plugin.\",\"howToHeading\":\"How to install \u0026 use Meshy for Maya\",\"installSteps\":{\"0\":\"Go to Resources in the MeshyAI website navigation and download the Maya plugin.\",\"1\":\"Unzip the downloaded file and place it in a local directory.\",\"2\":\"In Maya, open the Plug-in Manager, click Browse, and select the plugin file.\",\"3\":\"Set your main scene first, then import models from Meshy. Importing without a main scene set may cause errors.\"},\"overview\":\"Meshy for Maya is a free plugin that connects MeshyAI to your Maya workspace. Transfer models with one click via the DCC Bridge, with full support for animated models. Set your main scene before importing to ensure proper integration.\",\"quickFacts\":{\"0\":{\"label\":\"Type\",\"value\":\"Maya plugin\"},\"1\":{\"label\":\"Animated models\",\"value\":\"Supported\"},\"2\":{\"label\":\"Key requirement\",\"value\":\"Main scene must be set before importing\"}},\"requirements\":{\"0\":\"Autodesk Maya\",\"1\":\"A Meshy Pro account or above\",\"2\":\"Main scene must be set before importing\"}},\"Omniverse\":{\"faqs\":{\"0\":{\"a\":\"The bridge extension is free to download. Sending models through the DCC Bridge requires a Meshy Pro account or above.\",\"q\":\"Is the Meshy Omniverse Bridge free?\"},\"1\":{\"a\":\"The current documentation is tested with Isaac Sim 6.0.0. We recommend keeping Isaac Sim or your Omniverse Kit app updated for best compatibility.\",\"q\":\"Which Omniverse or Isaac Sim version is supported?\"},\"2\":{\"a\":\"Confirm Isaac Sim or your Kit app is running, Meshy Bridge is enabled, no other process is using port 5331, and an active USD stage is open.\",\"q\":\"Why can't Meshy connect to Omniverse?\"},\"3\":{\"a\":\"You can send body type, collision approximation, mass or density mode, physics material values, optional height, semantic class, and optional Wikidata QCode.\",\"q\":\"What Sim-Ready settings can I send?\"},\"4\":{\"a\":\"Send to OV/Isaac supports Meshy model types including animated models, but Smart Rig animated models are currently blocked in the webapp and should be downloaded and imported manually.\",\"q\":\"Are animated models supported?\"},\"5\":{\"a\":\"The current Meshy webapp Send to OV/Isaac flow is available on Windows only.\",\"q\":\"Is the bridge Windows-only?\"}},\"features\":{\"0\":{\"bullets\":{\"0\":\"Sends model URL, file format, and display name from Meshy to Omniverse\",\"1\":\"Extension downloads the asset and converts or references it in USD when needed\",\"2\":\"Imports the model under /World/model-slug in the active USD stage\",\"3\":\"Supports Meshy model types, including animated models supported by the current bridge flow\"},\"description\":\"Send completed Meshy models directly to an active Omniverse or Isaac Sim stage via the local bridge extension.\",\"title\":\"Bridge to Omniverse / Isaac Sim\"},\"1\":{\"bullets\":{\"0\":\"Choose dynamic, kinematic, or static body type\",\"1\":\"Select collision approximation such as convex hull, convex decomposition, bounding cube, or bounding sphere\",\"2\":\"Use Auto, Mass, or Density mass modes\",\"3\":\"Apply physics material values for static friction, dynamic friction, and restitution\"},\"description\":\"Configure simulation behavior before import for Isaac Sim and physics-driven OpenUSD workflows.\",\"title\":\"Sim-Ready Physics Settings\"},\"2\":{\"bullets\":{\"0\":\"Write semantic class labels and optional Wikidata QCode metadata\",\"1\":\"Set an optional real-world height override during import\",\"2\":\"Apply UsdPhysics collision and rigid-body APIs to imported assets\",\"3\":\"Keep the imported asset referenced inside the current USD stage\"},\"description\":\"Bring Meshy assets into USD stages with optional semantic metadata and scale controls for simulation workflows.\",\"title\":\"Semantic OpenUSD Import\"}},\"headline\":\"Send AI-generated 3D models directly into NVIDIA Omniverse or Isaac Sim with the Meshy Omniverse Bridge.\",\"howToHeading\":\"How to install \u0026 use Meshy Omniverse Bridge\",\"installSteps\":{\"0\":\"Download the Meshy Omniverse Bridge ZIP package.\",\"1\":\"In Isaac Sim or your Omniverse Kit app, open Window \u003e Extensions, choose Import Extension, then select the downloaded ZIP package.\",\"2\":\"Search for Meshy Bridge in the Extension Manager, enable it, and turn on Autoload if you want it to start automatically.\",\"3\":\"Open or create a USD stage, then choose Send to OV/Isaac from the DCC Bridge menu in Meshy.\"},\"overview\":\"Meshy Omniverse Bridge connects your Meshy workspace to an active Omniverse or Isaac Sim stage. It imports generated assets into OpenUSD workflows and can apply Sim-Ready body type, collision, physics material, height, semantic class, and optional Wikidata QCode settings during transfer.\",\"quickFacts\":{\"0\":{\"label\":\"Platform\",\"value\":\"NVIDIA Omniverse / Isaac Sim\"},\"1\":{\"label\":\"Bridge Type\",\"value\":\"Omniverse Kit extension\"},\"2\":{\"label\":\"Local Endpoint\",\"value\":\"127.0.0.1:5331\"},\"3\":{\"label\":\"Tested Version\",\"value\":\"Isaac Sim 6.0.0\"},\"4\":{\"label\":\"Account\",\"value\":\"Meshy Pro or above for DCC Bridge transfer\"}},\"requirements\":{\"0\":\"Windows for the current Meshy webapp bridge flow\",\"1\":\"Isaac Sim or an Omniverse Kit app running locally\",\"2\":\"An active USD stage before sending a model\",\"3\":\"Meshy Bridge extension enabled and listening on 127.0.0.1:5331\",\"4\":\"Meshy Pro account or above for DCC Bridge transfer\"}},\"OrcaSlicer\":{\"features\":{\"0\":{\"bullets\":{\"0\":\"Click Print → Send to OrcaSlicer from any model in your workspace\",\"1\":\"Model automatically downloads and opens in OrcaSlicer\",\"2\":\"Works with all Meshy-generated models and community models\",\"3\":\"No manual file downloading or importing required\"},\"description\":\"Send models from your Meshy workspace directly to OrcaSlicer with a single click.\",\"title\":\"One-Click Print Workflow\"},\"1\":{\"bullets\":{\"0\":\"Supports a wide range of FDM and resin printers\",\"1\":\"Advanced print settings and calibration tools\",\"2\":\"Active open-source community with frequent updates\"},\"description\":\"OrcaSlicer offers advanced slicing features and broad printer support built on an open-source foundation.\",\"title\":\"Open-Source Flexibility\"}},\"headline\":\"Send AI-generated 3D models straight to OrcaSlicer for advanced open-source slicing.\",\"installSteps\":{\"0\":\"Open a model in your Meshy workspace.\",\"1\":\"Click the Print menu and select Send to OrcaSlicer.\",\"2\":\"Confirm the browser prompt to open OrcaSlicer.\",\"3\":\"The model loads automatically — configure settings and print.\"},\"overview\":\"Meshy integrates with OrcaSlicer — a popular open-source slicer based on Bambu Studio — letting you transfer AI-generated models for slicing in one click. Select any model in your workspace, use the Print menu, and OrcaSlicer opens with your model ready to go.\",\"requirements\":{\"0\":\"OrcaSlicer installed on your computer\",\"1\":\"A Meshy Pro account or above\"}},\"RobloxStudio\":{\"faqs\":{\"0\":{\"a\":\"The Bridge app is free to download. However, uploading models to Roblox requires a Meshy Pro account or above.\",\"q\":\"Is the Meshy Roblox Bridge free?\"},\"1\":{\"a\":\"Models must be under 20 MB. For larger models, use the Remesh feature in Meshy first to reduce file size, then upload.\",\"q\":\"What is the model size limit?\"},\"2\":{\"a\":\"macOS and Windows. The Bridge is a native desktop app — there is no browser or mobile version.\",\"q\":\"Which operating systems are supported?\"},\"3\":{\"a\":\"macOS may block the app on first launch. Go to System Settings → Privacy \u0026 Security, find the blocked app entry, and click \\\"Open Anyway\\\".\",\"q\":\"Why is the app blocked on macOS?\"},\"4\":{\"a\":\"Uploaded models appear in your Roblox Creator Hub inventory and are immediately available to use in Roblox Studio.\",\"q\":\"Where do uploaded models appear after transfer?\"}},\"features\":{\"0\":{\"bullets\":{\"0\":\"One-click upload from Meshy workspace to Roblox inventory\",\"1\":\"GLB asset format for Roblox compatibility\",\"2\":\"Models are immediately available in Roblox Studio\",\"3\":\"Upload history tracking for easy management\"},\"description\":\"Upload models from your Meshy workspace directly to your Roblox Creator Hub inventory.\",\"title\":\"Direct Roblox Upload\"},\"1\":{\"bullets\":{\"0\":\"Open in Creator Hub to manage uploaded assets\",\"1\":\"Open in Studio to place models directly in your experience\",\"2\":\"Supports all Meshy-generated and community models\"},\"description\":\"Open uploaded models in Roblox Studio or the Creator Hub with one click.\",\"title\":\"Quick Access\"},\"2\":{\"bullets\":{\"0\":\"20 MB upload size limit — use Remesh to optimize larger models\",\"1\":\"Recommended: Generate → Remesh → Texture → Upload\",\"2\":\"Automatic model format handling\"},\"description\":\"Recommended workflow to ensure models meet the 20 MB upload limit.\",\"title\":\"Smart Workflow\"}},\"headline\":\"Upload AI-generated 3D models directly to your Roblox Creator Hub inventory with the Meshy Roblox Bridge.\",\"howToHeading\":\"How to download \u0026 use Meshy Roblox Bridge\",\"installSteps\":{\"0\":\"Go to Resources in the MeshyAI website navigation and download the Meshy Roblox Bridge.\",\"1\":\"Unzip and run the executable (macOS: Meshy Roblox Bridge, Windows: MeshyRobloxBridge.exe).\",\"2\":\"On macOS, you may need to allow the app via System Settings → Privacy \u0026 Security.\",\"3\":\"Connect your Roblox account in the bridge app, then send models from your Meshy workspace.\"},\"overview\":\"The Meshy Roblox Bridge is a standalone desktop app that uploads AI-generated models from your Meshy workspace to your Roblox Creator Hub inventory. Models become instantly available in Roblox Studio. Note: models must be under 20 MB — use the Remesh feature first for larger models.\",\"quickFacts\":{\"0\":{\"label\":\"Type\",\"value\":\"Standalone desktop app\"},\"1\":{\"label\":\"OS\",\"value\":\"macOS, Windows\"},\"2\":{\"label\":\"Plan required\",\"value\":\"Meshy Pro+\"},\"3\":{\"label\":\"File size limit\",\"value\":\"Under 20 MB\"}},\"requirements\":{\"0\":\"macOS or Windows\",\"1\":\"A Meshy Pro account or above\",\"2\":\"A Roblox account (global roblox.com)\",\"3\":\"Models must be under 20 MB (use Remesh for larger models)\"}},\"SnapmakerOrca\":{\"features\":{\"0\":{\"bullets\":{\"0\":\"Click Print → Send to Snapmaker Orca from any model in your workspace\",\"1\":\"Model automatically downloads and opens in Snapmaker Orca\",\"2\":\"Works with all Meshy-generated models and community models\",\"3\":\"No manual file downloading or importing required\"},\"description\":\"Send models from your Meshy workspace directly to Snapmaker Orca with a single click via the Print menu.\",\"title\":\"One-Click Print Workflow\"},\"1\":{\"bullets\":{\"0\":\"Native support for Snapmaker printer models\",\"1\":\"Pre-configured printer profiles for quick setup\",\"2\":\"Confirm the prompt to allow the transfer\"},\"description\":\"Optimized for Snapmaker's range of modular 3D printers.\",\"title\":\"Snapmaker Ecosystem\"}},\"headline\":\"Send AI-generated 3D models directly to Snapmaker Orca for one-click slicing on Snapmaker printers.\",\"installSteps\":{\"0\":\"Open a model in your Meshy workspace.\",\"1\":\"Click the Print menu and select Send to Snapmaker Orca.\",\"2\":\"Confirm the browser prompt to open Snapmaker Orca.\",\"3\":\"The model loads automatically — slice and print.\"},\"overview\":\"Meshy integrates with Snapmaker Orca — the official OrcaSlicer fork for Snapmaker 3D printers — so you can go from AI generation to print-ready slicing in seconds. Select any model in your Meshy workspace, hit Print, and it opens automatically in Snapmaker Orca ready to slice.\",\"requirements\":{\"0\":\"Snapmaker Orca installed on your computer\",\"1\":\"A Meshy Pro account or above\"}},\"ThreeDsMax\":{\"faqs\":{\"0\":{\"a\":\"Yes, free to download. A Meshy Pro account or above is required to use the DCC Bridge.\",\"q\":\"Is the Meshy 3ds Max plugin free?\"},\"1\":{\"a\":\"In 3ds Max, go to Scripting → Run Script, then navigate to the downloaded plugin file and open it. The Meshy window will appear automatically.\",\"q\":\"How do I install the plugin?\"},\"2\":{\"a\":\"Yes. Animated models are fully supported.\",\"q\":\"Does it support animated models?\"},\"3\":{\"a\":\"No. The plugin authenticates via your Meshy workspace automatically once connected.\",\"q\":\"Do I need to log in separately in the plugin?\"},\"4\":{\"a\":\"Please refer to the Requirements section on this page for the confirmed minimum version.\",\"q\":\"Which 3ds Max version is required?\"}},\"features\":{\"0\":{\"bullets\":{\"0\":\"Send models directly from your Meshy workspace to 3ds Max\",\"1\":\"Automatic model download and import\",\"2\":\"Works with any model in your workspace or the community gallery\",\"3\":\"No manual file downloading or importing required\"},\"description\":\"One-click model transfer from the MeshyAI webapp to 3ds Max via the DCC Bridge.\",\"title\":\"Bridge to 3ds Max\"},\"1\":{\"bullets\":{\"0\":\"Full animation data preserved on import\",\"1\":\"Animation playback via space key and Play Animation button\",\"2\":\"Supports all Meshy animation types\"},\"description\":\"Import animated models with full animation data preservation.\",\"title\":\"Animated Model Support\"}},\"headline\":\"Import AI-generated 3D models directly into Autodesk 3ds Max with the official Meshy plugin.\",\"howToHeading\":\"How to install \u0026 use Meshy for 3ds Max\",\"installSteps\":{\"0\":\"Go to Resources in the MeshyAI website navigation and download the 3ds Max plugin.\",\"1\":\"Unzip the downloaded file and place it in a local directory.\",\"2\":\"In 3ds Max, go to Scripting → Run Script and select the plugin file.\",\"3\":\"The Meshy plugin window opens automatically. Connect your account, then send your first model from Meshy to verify the import.\"},\"overview\":\"Meshy for 3ds Max is a free plugin that lets you import MeshyAI-generated models directly into 3ds Max. Use the DCC Bridge to transfer models with one click from your Meshy workspace, including full support for animated models with preserved animation data.\",\"quickFacts\":{\"0\":{\"label\":\"Type\",\"value\":\"Script/plugin\"},\"1\":{\"label\":\"Install method\",\"value\":\"Scripting → Run Script\"},\"2\":{\"label\":\"Animated models\",\"value\":\"Supported\"}},\"requirements\":{\"0\":\"Autodesk 3ds Max\",\"1\":\"A Meshy Pro account or above\"}},\"UltimakerCura\":{\"features\":{\"0\":{\"bullets\":{\"0\":\"Click Print → Send to Ultimaker Cura from any model in your workspace\",\"1\":\"Model automatically downloads and opens in Cura\",\"2\":\"Works with all Meshy-generated models and community models\",\"3\":\"May need to manually adjust model position depending on printer\"},\"description\":\"Send models from your Meshy workspace directly to Ultimaker Cura via the Print menu.\",\"title\":\"One-Click Print Workflow\"},\"1\":{\"bullets\":{\"0\":\"Supports 400+ FDM printer models out of the box\",\"1\":\"Extensive material and print profile library\",\"2\":\"Plugin marketplace for extended functionality\"},\"description\":\"Cura supports hundreds of FDM printers from various manufacturers.\",\"title\":\"Broad Printer Support\"}},\"headline\":\"Send AI-generated 3D models directly to Ultimaker Cura for versatile FDM printing.\",\"installSteps\":{\"0\":\"Open a model in your Meshy workspace.\",\"1\":\"Click the Print menu and select Send to Ultimaker Cura.\",\"2\":\"Confirm the browser prompt to open Cura.\",\"3\":\"Adjust model position if needed — slice and print.\"},\"overview\":\"Meshy integrates with Ultimaker Cura — one of the most popular open-source slicers for FDM printing. Send models from your workspace with one click. Note that depending on your printer model, you may need to manually adjust the model position after import.\",\"requirements\":{\"0\":\"Ultimaker Cura installed on your computer\",\"1\":\"A Meshy Pro account or above\"}},\"Unity\":{\"faqs\":{\"0\":{\"a\":\"Yes, free to download. A Meshy Pro account or above is required to use the DCC Bridge.\",\"q\":\"Is the Meshy Unity plugin free?\"},\"1\":{\"a\":\"Unity 6 (tested on 6000.0.45f1). We recommend keeping Unity updated for best compatibility.\",\"q\":\"Which Unity versions are supported?\"},\"2\":{\"a\":\"Yes. Animated models with full rig and animation data are supported and transfer correctly via the Bridge.\",\"q\":\"Does it support animated models?\"},\"3\":{\"a\":\"No. Log in to the Meshy web app in your browser and models transfer automatically — no second login required.\",\"q\":\"Do I need to log in separately inside the plugin?\"},\"4\":{\"a\":\"Yes, subject to the commercial use terms of your active Meshy plan. Check your plan details at meshy.ai/pricing.\",\"q\":\"Can I use assets generated with this plugin in commercial projects?\"}},\"features\":{\"0\":{\"bullets\":{\"0\":\"Send models directly from your Meshy workspace to Unity\",\"1\":\"Meshy menu appears in the Unity toolbar with a Bridge button\",\"2\":\"Automatic model download and import into your scene\",\"3\":\"Works with any model in your workspace or the community gallery\"},\"description\":\"One-click model transfer from the MeshyAI webapp to Unity via the DCC Bridge.\",\"title\":\"Bridge to Unity\"},\"1\":{\"bullets\":{\"0\":\"Full animation data preserved on import\",\"1\":\"Stand on Ground feature for automatic humanoid positioning\",\"2\":\"Supports all Meshy animation types\"},\"description\":\"Import animated models with full animation data preservation for game-ready assets.\",\"title\":\"Animated Model Support\"}},\"headline\":\"Import AI-generated 3D models directly into the Unity Editor with the official Meshy plugin.\",\"howToHeading\":\"How to install \u0026 use Meshy for Unity\",\"installSteps\":{\"0\":\"Go to Resources in the MeshyAI website navigation and download the Unity plugin (.unitypackage).\",\"1\":\"In Unity, import the package via Assets → Import Package → Custom Package.\",\"2\":\"Click Import to add the Meshy plugin to your project.\",\"3\":\"Use the Meshy menu in the toolbar to activate the Bridge. Send your first model from Meshy and verify it appears in the scene.\"},\"overview\":\"Meshy for Unity is a free plugin that brings one-click model import to the Unity Editor. Use the DCC Bridge to transfer any model from your Meshy workspace — including animated models with full animation data. The plugin adds a Meshy menu to your toolbar for instant access.\",\"quickFacts\":{\"0\":{\"label\":\"Type\",\"value\":\"Unity package (.unitypackage)\"},\"1\":{\"label\":\"Unity version\",\"value\":\"Unity 6 (tested on 6000.0.45f1)\"},\"2\":{\"label\":\"Account\",\"value\":\"Meshy Pro or above\"},\"3\":{\"label\":\"Animated models\",\"value\":\"Supported\"},\"4\":{\"label\":\"Best for\",\"value\":\"Game prototyping\"}},\"requirements\":{\"0\":\"Unity 6 (tested on 6000.0.45f1)\",\"1\":\"A Meshy Pro account or above\"}},\"UnrealEngine\":{\"faqs\":{\"0\":{\"a\":\"Yes, free to download. A Meshy Pro account or above is required to use the DCC Bridge.\",\"q\":\"Is the Meshy Unreal Engine plugin free?\"},\"1\":{\"a\":\"Unreal Engine 5.0 and later.\",\"q\":\"Which Unreal Engine versions are supported?\"},\"2\":{\"a\":\"Both options are supported. Copy the plugin folder to Engine/Plugins for engine-wide use, or [YourProject]/Plugins for project-specific installation.\",\"q\":\"Can I install the plugin at the engine level or project level?\"},\"3\":{\"a\":\"Yes. Animated models transfer with full animation data intact.\",\"q\":\"Does it support animated models?\"},\"4\":{\"a\":\"Go to Edit → Plugins in Unreal Engine, search for \\\"Meshy\\\", and make sure the plugin is enabled. Restart the editor if prompted.\",\"q\":\"The plugin isn't showing up after install — what should I check?\"}},\"features\":{\"0\":{\"bullets\":{\"0\":\"Send models directly from your Meshy workspace to Unreal Engine\",\"1\":\"Automatic model download and import into your project\",\"2\":\"Works with any model in your workspace or the community gallery\",\"3\":\"No manual file downloading or importing required\"},\"description\":\"One-click model transfer from the MeshyAI webapp to Unreal Engine via the DCC Bridge.\",\"title\":\"Bridge to Unreal\"},\"1\":{\"bullets\":{\"0\":\"Full animation data preserved on import\",\"1\":\"Animation playback via the play button\",\"2\":\"Supports all Meshy animation types\"},\"description\":\"Import animated models with full animation data preservation for game-ready assets.\",\"title\":\"Animated Model Support\"},\"2\":{\"bullets\":{\"0\":\"Engine-level install: available across all projects\",\"1\":\"Project-level install: isolated to a single project\",\"2\":\"Supports Unreal Engine 5.0 and later\"},\"description\":\"Install the plugin at the engine level for all projects, or per-project for isolated use.\",\"title\":\"Flexible Installation\"}},\"headline\":\"Import AI-generated 3D models directly into Unreal Engine with the official Meshy plugin.\",\"howToHeading\":\"How to install \u0026 use Meshy for Unreal Engine\",\"installSteps\":{\"0\":\"Go to Resources in the MeshyAI website navigation and download the Unreal plugin.\",\"1\":\"Choose an install location: Engine/Plugins (global) or YourProject/Plugins (per-project).\",\"2\":\"Unzip the plugin folder into the chosen Plugins directory.\",\"3\":\"Launch Unreal Engine. Confirm the plugin is enabled under Edit → Plugins, then send a model from Meshy to verify the import.\"},\"overview\":\"Meshy for Unreal Engine is a free plugin that enables one-click model import via the DCC Bridge. Supports animated models with full animation data. Install the plugin into either the Engine or your Project directory.\",\"quickFacts\":{\"0\":{\"label\":\"Type\",\"value\":\"Unreal plugin (ZIP)\"},\"1\":{\"label\":\"UE version\",\"value\":\"5.0+\"},\"2\":{\"label\":\"Install location\",\"value\":\"Engine-level or Project-level\"},\"3\":{\"label\":\"Animated models\",\"value\":\"Supported\"}},\"requirements\":{\"0\":\"Unreal Engine 5.0 or later\",\"1\":\"A Meshy Pro account or above\"}},\"ZBrush\":{\"faqs\":{\"0\":{\"a\":\"Yes, free to download. A Meshy Pro account or above is required to use the DCC Bridge.\",\"q\":\"Is the Meshy ZBrush plugin free?\"},\"1\":{\"a\":\"After installing, a Meshy palette appears in ZBrush. Send a model from Meshy, then click \\\"Import Pending\\\" in the palette to load it onto the canvas.\",\"q\":\"How do I import a model into ZBrush?\"},\"2\":{\"a\":\"No. ZBrush is a sculpting tool, so the plugin imports static OBJ geometry only. Animated and rigged sends are not supported.\",\"q\":\"Does it support animated models?\"},\"3\":{\"a\":\"ZBrush 2025.1 or later, since the plugin relies on the official ZBrush Python API. Older versions are not supported.\",\"q\":\"Which ZBrush version is required?\"},\"4\":{\"a\":\"Yes. The plugin runs on both macOS and Windows; the installer bundles its own Python runtime, so no separate Python install is needed.\",\"q\":\"Does it work on both macOS and Windows?\"}},\"features\":{\"0\":{\"bullets\":{\"0\":\"Send models directly from your Meshy workspace to ZBrush\",\"1\":\"Automatic model download and import as OBJ\",\"2\":\"Works with any model in your workspace or the community gallery\",\"3\":\"No manual file downloading or importing required\"},\"description\":\"One-click model transfer from the MeshyAI webapp to ZBrush via the DCC Bridge.\",\"title\":\"Bridge to ZBrush\"},\"1\":{\"bullets\":{\"0\":\"Imports clean OBJ geometry, ready to sculpt on the canvas\",\"1\":\"Base color map applied where available\",\"2\":\"Imported tools are saved into ZTools/Meshy for reuse\"},\"description\":\"Bring AI-generated meshes onto the ZBrush canvas as a clean starting point for sculpting.\",\"title\":\"Sculpt-Ready Geometry\"}},\"headline\":\"Import AI-generated 3D models directly into ZBrush with the official Meshy plugin.\",\"howToHeading\":\"How to install \u0026 use Meshy for ZBrush\",\"installSteps\":{\"0\":\"Go to Resources in the MeshyAI website navigation and download the ZBrush plugin.\",\"1\":\"Open the package and copy MeshyBridge.zsc and the MeshyBridgeData folder into ZBrush's ZData/ZPlugs64 directory.\",\"2\":\"On macOS, clear the Gatekeeper quarantine on MeshyBridgeData once (see the documentation), then restart ZBrush.\",\"3\":\"Open the Meshy palette in ZBrush, send a model from Meshy with Send to ZBrush, then click Import Pending to load it onto the canvas.\"},\"overview\":\"Meshy for ZBrush is a free plugin that connects MeshyAI to your ZBrush session. Transfer models with one click via the DCC Bridge — the model downloads in the background and imports onto the canvas as clean OBJ geometry when you click Import Pending. Runs on both macOS and Windows.\",\"quickFacts\":{\"0\":{\"label\":\"Type\",\"value\":\"ZBrush plugin\"},\"1\":{\"label\":\"Format\",\"value\":\"OBJ (static geometry)\"},\"2\":{\"label\":\"Animated models\",\"value\":\"Not supported\"},\"3\":{\"label\":\"Minimum version\",\"value\":\"ZBrush 2025.1+\"}},\"requirements\":{\"0\":\"ZBrush 2025.1 or later\",\"1\":\"macOS or Windows\",\"2\":\"A Meshy Pro account or above\"}}},\"FAQs\":{\"AgentCanDo\":{\"A\":\"The Meshy AI agent can handle the full 3D creation pipeline through natural language — from generating models based on text or image prompts, to applying AI textures, sending assets to slicer software, and even iterating on designs across multiple rounds. It's like having a 3D artist on your team that works at the speed of conversation.\",\"Q\":\"What can the AI agent do?\"},\"Free\":{\"A\":\"All Meshy plugins are free to download. The DCC Bridge feature for sending models requires a Meshy Pro account or above.\",\"Q\":\"Are these integrations free to use?\"},\"HowInstall\":{\"A\":\"You can download plugins from the Resources section in the top navigation of our website, then install them manually in your DCC tool. Each plugin has a detailed installation guide in our documentation — visit the documentation link on each integration card for step-by-step instructions.\",\"Q\":\"How do I install a Meshy plugin?\"},\"LoginSeparately\":{\"A\":\"Most plugins work directly from the Meshy web app — just log in and send models with one click. The Blender plugin requires a Meshy API key for its Bridge feature.\",\"Q\":\"Do I need to log in to the plugin separately?\"},\"NeedApiKey\":{\"A\":\"Yes, the Meshy MCP Server requires a Meshy API key to authenticate requests. You can get your API key from the Meshy dashboard under Settings → API Keys. The key is set as an environment variable when you install the MCP server.\",\"Q\":\"Do I need an API key for MCP?\"},\"RequestSupport\":{\"A\":\"Absolutely! If there's a 3D tool or platform you'd like Meshy to integrate with, contact us to submit your request. We're constantly expanding our ecosystem based on user feedback.\",\"Q\":\"Can I request support for a new tool?\"},\"SetupClaude\":{\"A\":\"Install the Meshy MCP Server by running 'claude mcp add meshy -- npx -y @meshy-ai/meshy-mcp-server -e MESHY_API_KEY=YOUR_KEY' in your terminal. Once installed, you can ask Claude to generate 3D models using natural language — no coding required.\",\"Q\":\"How do I set up Meshy with Claude?\"},\"WhatTools\":{\"A\":\"Meshy supports all major 3D software and creative tools — including Blender, Unity, Unreal Engine, 3ds Max, Maya, Godot, Roblox Studio, and popular 3D printing slicers like Bambu Studio and OrcaSlicer. If there's a tool you'd like us to support, feel free to contact us to request a new integration.\",\"Q\":\"What 3D tools does Meshy integrate with?\"}},\"LearnMore\":\"Learn More\",\"OrbitHero\":{\"AgentTagline\":\"Powering {name} by {company} with Meshy AI 3D Generation.\",\"ViewDetails\":\"View details\"},\"Page\":{\"AnchorAgent\":\"Agent Integrations\",\"AnchorDCC\":\"DCC Integrations\",\"BuildYourOwn\":{\"ApiDocs\":\"API Docs\",\"ContactLink\":\"Contact us\",\"DescriptionPart1\":\"Use the Meshy REST API to programmatically generate 3D models from text or images, apply AI texturing, and more. Need support for a new tool?\",\"DescriptionPart2\":\"to request new integrations.\",\"Heading\":\"Build your own integration\",\"LearnMore\":\"Learn More\"},\"CTAButton\":\"Find Your Integration\",\"CTATitle\":\"Connect Meshy to your creative stack.\",\"CategoryDesc\":{\"API\":\"Programmatic access to all of Meshy's AI 3D generation capabilities.\",\"GameEngines\":\"Create game-ready 3D assets powered by AI within your game development environment.\",\"PhysicsSimulation\":\"Send Meshy-generated assets into simulation workflows with OpenUSD stages, physics properties, collisions, and semantic labels.\",\"Slicers\":\"Export AI-generated models to popular slicing software for 3D printing.\",\"ThreeDModeling\":\"Generate and import AI 3D models directly inside your favorite modeling software.\"},\"DiscoverDescription\":\"Supercharge your 3D workflow with native plugins for modeling, game engines, and 3D printing tools.\",\"DiscoverHeading\":\"All DCC integrations\",\"DiscoverLabel\":\"Discover DCC Integrations\",\"FAQTitle\":\"Frequently Asked Questions\",\"HeroDescription\":\"Native plugins for 3D tools and game engines, AI agents via the MCP protocol, plus a REST API for custom workflows.\",\"HeroLabel\":\"Integrations\",\"HeroTitlePart1\":\"Connect Meshy to your creative tools\",\"HeroTitlePart2\":\"and your AI\",\"Highlight\":{\"Ecosystem\":{\"Description\":\"From Blender to Unity to 3D printers — 13+ integrations and growing, plus a REST API for custom workflows.\",\"Title\":\"Broad ecosystem\"},\"FullAsset\":{\"Description\":\"Send any type of asset — untextured meshes, PBR-textured models, and rigged animations. Everything transfers seamlessly.\",\"Title\":\"Full asset support\"},\"OneClick\":{\"Description\":\"Send AI-generated 3D models directly to your DCC tools with one click — no downloading, no manual importing.\",\"Title\":\"One-click transfer\"}},\"UseCases\":{\"Description\":\"See how teams use Meshy integrations across 3D printing, modeling, and game development pipelines.\",\"GameDevDescription\":\"Import AI 3D assets directly into Unity, Unreal Engine, Godot, and Roblox Studio for game-ready content.\",\"GameDevTitle\":\"Game Development\",\"Heading\":\"Powering real workflows\",\"Label\":\"Use Cases\",\"ThreeDModelingDescription\":\"Bridge AI-generated assets into Blender, Maya, and 3ds Max for further refinement, texturing, and rendering.\",\"ThreeDPrintingDescription\":\"Generate AI models and send them straight to your slicer — Bambu Studio, OrcaSlicer, Creality Print, and more.\"},\"WhyDescription\":\"From plugin to production — Meshy integrations are built to fit naturally into your existing 3D workflow.\",\"WhyHeading\":\"Seamless by design\",\"WhyLabel\":\"Why DCC Integrations\"}},\"Landing\":{\"VsHero\":{\"BreadcrumbCurrent\":\"Meshy vs {competitor}\",\"Compare\":\"Compare\",\"Home\":\"Home\",\"LastUpdated\":\"Last updated: {date}\",\"StartCreating\":\"Start Creating 3D Model\",\"TrustedByCreators\":\"Trusted by creators from leading companies worldwide\"},\"VsHunyuan3D\":{\"AtAGlance\":{\"FullCommercial\":\"Full commercial rights\",\"GeoRestricted\":\"Geo-restricted (not EU/UK/KR)\",\"LinuxGPU\":\"Linux + 10–29GB GPU\",\"NoneHosted\":\"None (hosted)\",\"NoneWebBased\":\"None (web-based)\"},\"Detailed\":{\"API\":{\"Competitor\":\"Tencent Cloud Hunyuan 3D API for hosted inference (credit-based, with PBR/multi-view/LowPoly add-ons). Open-source inference runs locally via Python after downloading model weights from Hugging Face.\",\"Meshy\":\"REST API with SDKs for Python and Node.js, API Playground, webhooks, batch processing, and versioned endpoints.\",\"Title\":\"API \u0026 Developer Tools\"},\"Animation\":{\"Competitor\":\"No open-source rigging or animation pipeline. The hosted Hunyuan 3D Studio mentions mesh manipulation, but no public rigging or motion library is documented.\",\"Meshy\":\"Full animation suite: auto-rigging for humanoid and quadruped, 500+ motion presets, custom keyframe animation, direct export to Unity and Unreal Engine.\"},\"Enterprise\":{\"Competitor\":\"At launch, the hosted Hunyuan 3D Engine listed 150+ enterprise customers in Mainland China including Unity China and Bambu Lab, but no public SOC 2, ISO 27001, or GDPR certifications are listed.\",\"Meshy\":\"Team workspace, role-based access control, SOC 2 Type II + ISO 27001 + GDPR certified, dedicated Enterprise support.\",\"Title\":\"Enterprise \u0026 Team Features\"},\"ImageQuality\":{\"Competitor\":\"Research-grade image-to-3D foundation model. Hunyuan3D 2.1 (OSS, latest open release) ships 3.3B shape + 2B paint params. Hunyuan 3D 3.0 (Sept 2025) and Hunyuan 3D 3.1 (Nov 2025) power Tencent's hosted engine with higher resolution, high-resolution PBR textures, and up to 8-view input. GLB/OBJ output only.\",\"Meshy\":\"PBR textures with 5 map types (Albedo, Normal, Roughness, Metallic, AO), multi-view reconstruction, built-in 3D viewer, and export to 10+ formats.\",\"Title\":\"Image to 3D Quality\"},\"Plugins\":{\"Competitor\":\"Hosted Hunyuan 3D Engine ships Blender, Unity, and Unreal plugins. Open-source releases offer a Blender addon for the local API server; everything else is manual GLB/OBJ import.\",\"Meshy\":\"Native plugins for Blender, Unity, Unreal Engine, Maya, 3DS Max, Godot, and Roblox. One-click import/export.\"},\"Pricing\":{\"Competitor\":\"Open-source model weights are free to download. Running them requires a Linux server with a 10–29GB NVIDIA GPU — that's the hidden cost. Hosted Tencent Cloud API runs on credits (~$0.014–$0.02 per credit; ~25 credits per standard image-to-3D call).\",\"Meshy\":\"SaaS subscription — see meshy.ai/pricing for current plans. No infrastructure required — compute runs on Meshy's cloud. Free tier with 100 credits/month.\",\"Title\":\"Cost of Use\"},\"TextTo3D\":{\"Competitor\":\"Both the open-source 2.1 release and the hosted Hunyuan 3D Engine support text and image input. The hosted engine also adds multi-view and sketch input.\",\"Meshy\":\"Natural language prompts with 500+ style presets — realistic, anime, cartoon, voxel, sculpture. Full textured model in under 60 seconds.\"}},\"Faq\":{\"API\":{\"A\":\"Yes — Tencent Cloud offers a hosted Hunyuan 3D API with credit-based billing (approximately $0.014–$0.02 per credit, with 25 credits per standard image-to-3D call and additional credits for PBR, multi-view, or LowPoly add-ons). The open-source releases also provide Python inference scripts that you can host yourself. Meshy provides a full REST API with webhooks, batch processing, and versioned endpoints, plus an in-product API Playground.\",\"Q\":\"Does Hunyuan3D have a hosted API?\"},\"Animation\":{\"A\":\"The open-source Hunyuan3D releases output static meshes only — there is no built-in rigging, motion library, or animation workflow in the public repositories. The hosted Hunyuan 3D Studio mentions mesh manipulation at a high level but does not document a rigging system. Meshy includes auto-rigging for humanoid and quadruped characters, a library of 500+ preset animations, and direct export of rigged FBX/GLB to Unity, Unreal Engine, Godot, and Roblox.\",\"Q\":\"Does Hunyuan3D support animation or rigging?\"},\"Commercial\":{\"A\":\"Not unconditionally. Hunyuan3D 2.1 is released under the Tencent Hunyuan 3D 2.1 Community License — not a standard open-source license. The terms include: (1) the license does not apply in the European Union, United Kingdom, or South Korea; (2) if your product or service has more than 1 million monthly active users on the release date, you must request a separate license from Tencent; (3) you cannot use the model or its outputs to train any other AI model. Meshy's paid plans include full commercial ownership with no such restrictions and are available globally.\",\"Q\":\"Is Hunyuan3D free to use commercially?\"},\"Formats\":{\"A\":\"Hunyuan3D exports GLB and OBJ formats with PBR materials. The hosted engine documentation also lists GLB and OBJ as the primary outputs. FBX, STL, USDZ, and 3MF are not natively exported. Meshy exports FBX, GLB, OBJ, STL, USDZ, 3MF, and BLEND.\",\"Q\":\"What file formats does Hunyuan3D export?\"},\"FreePlan\":{\"A\":\"Yes. Meshy offers a free tier with 100 credits per month, no credit card required, which is enough for about 10 full generations including PBR texturing. See meshy.ai/pricing for current plan details. Hunyuan3D's open-source weights are free to download, but you need to supply your own GPU; the hosted Hunyuan 3D consumer app offers 20 free generations per day.\",\"Q\":\"Does Meshy offer a free plan?\"},\"GPU\":{\"A\":\"For the open-source Hunyuan3D 2.1, yes — the official GitHub README documents 10GB VRAM for shape generation, 21GB for texturing, and 29GB for shape + texture in one pass. It also requires CUDA 12.4, Python 3.10, and Linux (Windows and macOS are not officially supported for the full pipeline). The hosted Hunyuan 3D Engine runs on Tencent's cloud and needs no local GPU. Meshy runs entirely in the browser on Windows, Mac, Linux, iOS, and Android with no local hardware requirements at all.\",\"Q\":\"Do I need a GPU or special hardware to use Hunyuan3D?\"},\"GameDev\":{\"A\":\"Meshy is the stronger choice for game developers. It offers 500+ preset animations, auto-rigging, full PBR textures, and native plugins for Unity, Unreal Engine, Godot, and Roblox. Hunyuan3D's open-source releases output static GLB/OBJ meshes with no rigging or animation, so integrating them into a game pipeline requires substantial additional work in Blender, Maya, or a custom toolchain.\",\"Q\":\"Which is better for game development?\"},\"GeoRestriction\":{\"A\":\"It depends on which surface you use. For the open-source Hunyuan3D 2.1, the answer is no: the Community License explicitly states it does not apply in the EU, UK, or South Korea, and prohibits using, reproducing, modifying, distributing, or displaying outputs outside the licensed territory. For the hosted Hunyuan 3D 3.1, the situation is legally unresolved — Tencent Cloud's separate API Terms of Service do not exclude these regions, and Tencent contracts with EU and Korean users through Tencent Cloud Europe B.V. and Tencent Korea Yuhan Hoesa. However, the 2.1 Community License explicitly defines 'Hosted Service' and claims to govern hosted use, so the two documents conflict. Until Tencent publishes clarifying guidance, EU/UK/KR commercial use of hosted Hunyuan 3D carries unresolved license risk. Meshy is available globally under a single commercial license with no territorial restrictions.\",\"Q\":\"Can I use Hunyuan3D in the EU, UK, or South Korea?\"},\"Install\":{\"A\":\"Installing Hunyuan3D 2.1 locally requires a Linux machine with an NVIDIA GPU (10GB+ VRAM for shape, 21GB for texture, 29GB for the full pipeline), CUDA 12.4, Python 3.10, and PyTorch 2.5.1. The official steps are: clone the Tencent-Hunyuan/Hunyuan3D-2.1 GitHub repository, install dependencies (including custom rasterizer wheels), download model weights from Hugging Face, then run the provided Python scripts or the Gradio demo. The hosted Hunyuan 3D Engine at 3d.hunyuan.tencent.com avoids installation but requires a Tencent account and consumer access is gated by region. If you want to skip installation entirely, Meshy generates the same type of 3D models directly in your browser — no downloads, no GPU, no configuration.\",\"Q\":\"How do I install and use Hunyuan3D?\"},\"Ownership\":{\"A\":\"On Meshy's paid plans, you own the outputs entirely — full commercial rights, no attribution required, available globally. On the free plan, assets are licensed under CC BY 4.0. Hunyuan3D's situation is more complex: outputs are subject to the Tencent Hunyuan 3D 2.1 Community License, which restricts commercial use in the EU, UK, and South Korea and prohibits using outputs to train competing models. If you plan to sell assets globally, Meshy's paid plan is the simpler, legally clearer option.\",\"Q\":\"Who owns the 3D models I generate?\"},\"Printing\":{\"A\":\"Meshy is the better choice for 3D printing. Meshy generates optimized, watertight meshes and exports STL, 3MF, and OBJ with one-click Bambu Studio integration and a 97% slicer pass rate. Hunyuan3D exports GLB or OBJ with no native slicer integration, no watertight mesh guarantees, and no print-specific tooling.\",\"Q\":\"How does Hunyuan3D compare for 3D printing?\"},\"Retexture\":{\"A\":\"No — Hunyuan3D generates textures as part of its own image-to-mesh pipeline. It cannot apply new PBR textures to a mesh you already have. Meshy's AI Texturing engine generates full PBR maps on any mesh, including assets you didn't create in Meshy.\",\"Q\":\"Can Hunyuan3D retexture an existing mesh?\"},\"TextTo3D\":{\"A\":\"It depends which surface you use. The hosted Hunyuan 3D Engine supports text, image, multi-view, and sketch inputs. The open-source Hunyuan3D 2.1 release is primarily an image-to-3D model — text input typically routes through an upstream text-to-image model first, then feeds the generated image into the 3D pipeline. Meshy supports both text-to-3D and image-to-3D natively in the same browser-based workflow.\",\"Q\":\"Does Hunyuan3D support text-to-3D generation?\"},\"Versions\":{\"A\":\"Hunyuan3D 2.0 (Jan 2025) introduced the two-stage shape + paint pipeline. Hunyuan3D 2.1 (Jun 2025) is the latest open-source release — 3.3B shape + 2B paint parameters, first to ship full PBR weights and training code. Hunyuan 3D 2.5, 3.0, and 3.1 are hosted-only and not open-sourced: 3.0 (Sept 2025) reached 1536³ resolution, and 3.1 (Nov 2025) added 8-view input, watertight meshes, cleaner topology, and 4K PBR textures. Meshy ships a single production model — Meshy 6 — covering text/image input, PBR texturing, animation, and engine export in one workflow.\",\"Q\":\"What's the difference between Hunyuan3D 2.1, 3.0, and 3.1?\"},\"WhatIs\":{\"A\":\"Hunyuan3D is Tencent's flagship open-source 3D foundation model family, with a hosted Hunyuan 3D Engine on top. The latest open-source release, Hunyuan3D 2.1 (June 2025), takes a single image or a few multi-view images and outputs a textured 3D mesh in GLB or OBJ format, using a two-stage Hunyuan3D-DiT (shape) + Hunyuan3D-Paint (texture) pipeline. The hosted engine — currently running Hunyuan 3D 3.1 (Nov 2025) — adds higher resolution, 4K PBR, and 8-view input but is closed-source. Running 2.1 locally requires a Linux machine with a 10–29GB NVIDIA GPU, CUDA 12.4, and Python 3.10. The Community License excludes the EU, UK, and South Korea.\",\"Q\":\"What is Hunyuan3D?\"}},\"Feature\":{\"AITexturing\":\"AI Texturing\",\"AnimationRigging\":\"Animation \u0026 Rigging\",\"EnterpriseFeatures\":\"Enterprise Features\",\"ImageTo3D\":\"Image to 3D\",\"License\":\"Commercial License\",\"PluginEcosystem\":\"Plugin Ecosystem\",\"SetupRequired\":\"Setup Required\",\"TextTo3D\":\"Text to 3D\"},\"Features\":{\"Animation\":{\"CTA\":\"Browse the Animation Library\",\"Description\":\"Meshy includes auto-rigging and a library of 500+ preset animations — walk cycles, attacks, idles, and more. Export rigged, animated characters directly to Unity, Unreal Engine, Godot, or Roblox in one click. Hunyuan3D's open-source releases output static meshes only, with no built-in rigging or motion library.\",\"Label\":\"Animation\",\"Title\":\"500+ Ready-to-Use Animations, Out of the Box\"},\"ImageTo3D\":{\"CTA\":\"Try Image to 3D\",\"Description\":\"Meshy converts single images or multi-view photos into fully textured, PBR-ready 3D models. Unlike Hunyuan3D, Meshy also supports retexturing existing assets — giving you full control over any mesh you upload.\",\"Title\":\"Turn Any Photo Into a 3D Model\"},\"Printing\":{\"CTA\":\"See 3D Printing Workflow\",\"Description\":\"Meshy generates optimized, watertight meshes ready for slicing — no cleanup in Blender or Meshmixer needed. Export in STL, 3MF, or OBJ and send directly to Bambu Studio with one click. Hunyuan3D exports GLB or OBJ with no print-specific tooling or slicer integrations.\",\"Label\":\"3D Printing\",\"Title\":\"From Idea to Print-Ready in Minutes\"},\"TextTo3D\":{\"CTA\":\"Try Text to 3D\",\"Description\":\"Type a description, get a textured 3D model in under 60 seconds. Meshy supports 500+ art style presets across realistic, anime, cartoon, voxel, and sculpture. Hunyuan3D's open-source release is image-to-3D primarily — text input goes through an upstream text-to-image step.\",\"Title\":\"From Prompt to Production-Ready 3D\"},\"Texturing\":{\"CTA\":\"Retexture a Mesh\",\"Description\":\"Meshy generates full PBR texture maps — Albedo, Normal, Roughness, Metallic, and AO — on any mesh, including models you didn't create in Meshy. Hunyuan3D's texturing is tied to its own mesh output and doesn't support retexturing arbitrary uploaded geometry.\",\"Label\":\"Texturing\",\"Title\":\"AI Texture Generation on Any 3D Mesh\"}},\"Hero\":{\"Description\":\"Meshy is a browser-based AI 3D platform with animation, rigging, and 7 engine plugins. Tencent Hunyuan3D ships open-source 2.1 weights for self-hosting on a 10–29GB GPU plus a hosted Hunyuan 3D 3.1 engine. See where each one wins for game devs, 3D printing, and production pipelines.\",\"LastUpdated\":\"May 2026\",\"ReadTime\":\"8 min read\",\"TitleHighlight\":\"Which AI 3D Generator\",\"TitlePart1\":\"Meshy vs. Hunyuan3D:\",\"TitlePart3\":\"Should You Choose?\"},\"NA\":\"N/A\",\"None\":\"None\",\"NotApplicable\":\"Not applicable\",\"NotSupported\":\"Not supported\",\"RelatedBlog\":{\"GameAssets\":\"Best AI Tools for 3D Game Assets (2026 Compared)\",\"PrintReady\":\"What Actually Makes an AI 3D Model Print-Ready?\",\"Printing\":\"Best AI Tools for 3D Printing in 2026: Tested \u0026 Compared\"},\"RelatedComparisons\":{\"Trellis2\":{\"Description\":\"Open-source 3D generation compared\",\"Title\":\"Meshy vs Trellis 2\"},\"Tripo\":{\"Description\":\"Compare two leading AI 3D generation platforms\",\"Title\":\"Meshy vs Tripo\"}},\"Table\":{\"Animation\":{\"AutoRigging\":\"Auto-Rigging\",\"AutoRiggingMeshy\":\"Humanoid \u0026 quadruped\",\"Export\":\"Rigged Character Export\",\"ExportMeshy\":\"Animated FBX/GLB with full skeleton \u0026 weights\",\"Library\":\"Animation Library\",\"LibraryMeshy\":\"500+ presets (walk, run, idle, combat, dance, emotes)\",\"Title\":\"Animation \u0026 Motion\"},\"Generation\":{\"ArtStylesCompetitor\":\"No native style presets — output follows the input image\",\"ArtStylesFeature\":\"Art Styles\",\"ArtStylesMeshy\":\"Realistic, Anime, Cartoon, Voxel, Sculpture\",\"ImageTo3DCompetitor\":\"Single \u0026 multi-view (up to 4)\",\"ImageTo3DFeature\":\"Image-to-3D\",\"ImageTo3DMeshy\":\"Single \u0026 multi-view\",\"LatestModelCompetitor\":\"Hunyuan3D 2.1 (OSS) / Hunyuan 3D 3.1 (hosted)\",\"LatestModelFeature\":\"Latest Model\",\"PlatformCompetitor\":\"Linux only for OSS 2.1; Windows / macOS via hosted 3.1 engine\",\"PlatformFeature\":\"Platform Support\",\"PlatformMeshy\":\"All platforms via browser\",\"SetupCompetitor\":\"Linux, NVIDIA GPU 10–29GB VRAM, CUDA 12.4, Python 3.10 (OSS)\",\"SetupMeshy\":\"None — fully browser-based\",\"TextTo3DCompetitor\":\"Natural language \u0026 image prompts (OSS 2.1 + hosted engine)\",\"TextTo3DFeature\":\"Text-to-3D\",\"TextTo3DMeshy\":\"Natural language \u0026 image prompts\",\"TimeCompetitor\":\"Depends on local GPU for Hunyuan3D 2.1 (OSS, 24GB+ VRAM); hosted Hunyuan 3D 3.1 runs on Tencent's cloud\",\"TimeFeature\":\"Generation Time\",\"TimeMeshy\":\"~1 min (cloud, no GPU required)\",\"Title\":\"3D Generation\"},\"Integrations\":{\"API\":\"Hosted API\",\"APICompetitor\":\"Tencent Cloud API (credit-based) for hosted engine; self-hosted Python inference for OSS\",\"APIMeshy\":\"Full REST API with Playground \u0026 versioned endpoints\",\"CustomPipeline\":\"Custom Pipeline Integration\",\"CustomPipelineCompetitor\":\"Python library on Hugging Face (self-hosted) or Tencent Cloud SDK\",\"CustomPipelineMeshy\":\"REST API + webhooks + batch processing\",\"ExportFormats\":\"Export Formats\",\"ExportFormatsCompetitor\":\"GLB and OBJ only\",\"Plugins\":\"Engine \u0026 DCC Plugins\",\"PluginsCompetitor\":\"Blender, Unity, Unreal Engine (hosted engine only)\",\"Printing\":\"3D Printing Integration\",\"PrintingCompetitor\":\"No native slicer integration; GLB/OBJ export only\",\"PrintingMeshy\":\"Native Bambu Studio one-click send; STL/3MF for any slicer\",\"Security\":\"Security Certifications\",\"SecurityCompetitor\":\"Not publicly listed for hosted engine; N/A for self-hosted OSS\",\"TeamMgmt\":\"Team \u0026 User Management\",\"TeamMgmtCompetitor\":\"Limited team support on hosted engine; none for OSS\",\"TeamMgmtMeshy\":\"Team workspace, multi-user access, role-based permissions\",\"Title\":\"Integrations \u0026 Workflow\"},\"Pricing\":{\"AssetRetention\":\"Asset Retention\",\"AssetRetentionCompetitor\":\"Local storage for OSS; hosted engine retention per Tencent Cloud policy\",\"AssetRetentionMeshy\":\"3 days (Pro/Studio) / Forever (Enterprise)\",\"CommercialLicense\":\"Commercial License\",\"CommercialLicenseCompetitor\":\"Tencent Hunyuan 3D Community License — requires Tencent approval above 1M MAU; cannot be used to train competing models\",\"CommercialLicenseMeshy\":\"Full ownership on paid; CC BY 4.0 on free\",\"CostModel\":\"Cost Model\",\"CostModelCompetitor\":\"Pay-per-credit (~$0.014–$0.02/credit) on hosted API, or supply your own GPU server\",\"CostModelMeshy\":\"SaaS subscription — no infrastructure needed\",\"EntryPlan\":\"Entry Paid Plan\",\"EntryPlanCompetitor\":\"Credit packs from $15 (1,000 credits) on Tencent Cloud\",\"EntryPlanMeshy\":\"Pro plan\",\"FreeAccess\":\"Free Access\",\"FreeAccessCompetitor\":\"20 free generations/day (hosted); model weights free to download (OSS)\",\"FreeAccessMeshy\":\"100 monthly credits (no credit card)\",\"GeoAvailability\":\"Geographic Availability\",\"GeoAvailabilityCompetitor\":\"OSS 2.1: license excludes the EU, UK, and South Korea. Hosted 3.1: Tencent Cloud terms do not exclude these regions, but the parent Community License purports to cover hosted use — EU/UK/KR commercial status is legally unresolved.\",\"GeoAvailabilityMeshy\":\"Available globally\",\"Title\":\"Pricing \u0026 Access\"},\"Quality\":{\"AITexturingCompetitor\":\"Textures generated as part of mesh output; no standalone retexture mode\",\"AITexturingMeshy\":\"Dedicated AI Texturing engine — retexture any mesh you upload\",\"AITexturingStandalone\":\"AI Texturing (standalone)\",\"HardSurface\":\"Hard-Surface Accuracy\",\"HardSurfaceCompetitor\":\"Hard edges and sharp silhouettes often need manual cleanup\",\"HardSurfaceMeshy\":\"Sharp edges and clean silhouettes (Meshy 6)\",\"MeshTopology\":\"Mesh Topology\",\"MeshTopologyCompetitor\":\"Sparse voxel representation; outputs require retopology for production\",\"MeshTopologyMeshy\":\"Clean meshes with good edge flow\",\"OutputResolution\":\"Output Resolution\",\"OutputResolutionCompetitor\":\"Up to 1536³ on Hunyuan 3D 3.1 (hosted); lower on Hunyuan3D 2.1 (OSS), depending on GPU\",\"OutputResolutionMeshy\":\"High-quality textured meshes, optimized for export\",\"PBRSupport\":\"PBR Material Support\",\"PBRSupportCompetitor\":\"Albedo, Metallic, Roughness on Hunyuan3D 2.1 (OSS); bump and high-resolution maps on Hunyuan 3D 3.1 (hosted)\",\"PBRSupportMeshy\":\"Full PBR (Albedo, Normal, Metallic, Roughness, AO)\",\"PrintReadiness\":\"3D Print-Readiness\",\"PrintReadinessCompetitor\":\"GLB/OBJ export only; no print-specific tooling or slicer integration\",\"PrintReadinessMeshy\":\"97% slicer pass rate; Bambu Studio integration; 3MF export\",\"Title\":\"Output Quality\"},\"Ratings\":{\"Community\":\"Community Size\",\"CommunityCompetitor\":\"13.8K+ GitHub stars; 3M+ Hugging Face downloads across Hunyuan3D models\",\"CommunityMeshy\":\"10M+ users worldwide\",\"Enterprise\":\"Enterprise Readiness\",\"EnterpriseCompetitor\":\"At launch, 150+ enterprise customers in Mainland China; no public security certifications listed\",\"EnterpriseMeshy\":\"SOC 2 + ISO 27001 certified, dedicated support\",\"G2\":\"G2 Rating\",\"G2Competitor\":\"Not listed — research model + early hosted product\",\"Support\":\"Customer Support\",\"SupportCompetitor\":\"GitHub Issues; Tencent Cloud ticket support for hosted engine\",\"SupportMeshy\":\"Email + Help Center + dedicated Enterprise support\",\"Title\":\"Ratings \u0026 Trust\",\"Trustpilot\":\"Trustpilot Rating\",\"TrustpilotCompetitor\":\"Not listed\"}},\"Tldr\":{\"CompetitorPitch\":\"You're an ML researcher or engineer who needs open-source model weights for a custom self-hosted pipeline, have access to a 10–29GB GPU server.\",\"CompetitorSummary\":\"is Tencent's 3D model family, split into an open-source line (latest Hunyuan3D 2.1, requires a Linux server with a 10–29GB NVIDIA GPU) and a hosted engine (currently Hunyuan 3D 3.1, launched globally in November 2025). Best fit if you need open model weights for research, or you want a credit-based hosted API and operate outside the EU, UK, and South Korea, where Tencent's Community License restricts commercial use.\",\"MeshyPitch\":\"You need a complete 3D pipeline today: generation, texturing, rigging, animation, and engine integrations, with no Linux server or GPU required.\",\"MeshySummary\":\"is a cloud AI 3D platform that runs in any browser, with no GPU or install required. Generate from text or image, texture with PBR maps, auto-rig characters, and animate with 500+ presets. Export to Unity, Unreal, Blender, Maya, Godot, Roblox, or 3D slicers in one click. SOC 2 and ISO 27001 certified, 10M+ users worldwide.\"},\"WhoShouldChoose\":{\"Competitor\":{\"GPU\":\"You already have a Linux server with a 10–29GB NVIDIA GPU and prefer full control over your infrastructure\",\"ML\":\"You're an ML researcher or engineer who needs an open-source 3D foundation model to integrate into a custom self-hosted pipeline\",\"PBR\":\"Your priority is high-fidelity PBR texture output for organic shapes, and you're comfortable doing your own retopology, rigging, and engine integration\",\"SelfHost\":\"You're operating inside Tencent's licensed territories and are comfortable with the Community License terms (1M MAU cap, no training of competing models)\",\"Weights\":\"You need access to open model weights for research, fine-tuning, or internal experimentation — Hunyuan3D 2.1 ships both weights and training code\"},\"Meshy\":{\"API\":\"You need a production-grade hosted API — Meshy provides a full REST API with webhooks, batch processing, and versioned endpoints\",\"Animation\":\"Animation matters — Meshy includes auto-rigging and 500+ preset animations; Hunyuan3D's open-source releases output static meshes only\",\"GPU\":\"You don't have a Linux server or a 10–29GB NVIDIA GPU — Meshy runs entirely in the browser with no installation or hardware required\",\"License\":\"You're based in the EU, UK, or South Korea, or you ship products there — Hunyuan3D's Community License excludes those territories; Meshy's commercial license is global\",\"Plugins\":\"You need broad engine and DCC coverage — Meshy ships native plugins for Blender, Unity, Unreal Engine, Maya, 3DS Max, Godot, and Roblox\"}}},\"VsPeopleChoose\":{\"Title\":\"What Switchers Say\"},\"VsStats\":{\"CommunityBenchmark\":\"Community Benchmark\",\"CommunityEloRankings\":\"Community ELO Rankings\"},\"VsTrellis2\":{\"AtAGlance\":{\"FreePaidPlans\":\"Free + paid plans\",\"FreeSelfHosted\":\"Free (self-hosted)\",\"LinuxGPU\":\"Linux + 24GB GPU\",\"NoneWebBased\":\"None (web-based)\"},\"Detailed\":{\"API\":{\"Competitor\":\"No hosted API. Python inference via Hugging Face model download. Suitable for custom ML pipelines on self-hosted infrastructure.\",\"Meshy\":\"REST API with SDKs for Python and Node.js, API Playground, webhooks, batch processing, and versioned endpoints.\",\"Title\":\"API \u0026 Developer Tools\"},\"Animation\":{\"Competitor\":\"Not supported. Trellis 2 outputs static meshes only.\",\"Meshy\":\"Full animation suite: auto-rigging for humanoid and quadruped, 500+ motion presets, custom keyframe animation, direct export to Unity and Unreal Engine.\"},\"Enterprise\":{\"Competitor\":\"Not applicable — Trellis 2 is a research model with no SaaS product, no team management, and no enterprise support.\",\"Meshy\":\"Team workspace, role-based access control, SOC 2 Type II + ISO 27001 + GDPR certified, dedicated Enterprise support.\",\"Title\":\"Enterprise \u0026 Team Features\"},\"ImageQuality\":{\"Competitor\":\"Research-grade image-to-3D model at 4B parameters. Handles complex topology including non-manifold geometry and internal structures. Up to 1536³ voxel resolution on high-end GPUs. GLB output only.\",\"Meshy\":\"PBR textures with 5 map types (Albedo, Normal, Roughness, Metallic, AO), multi-view reconstruction, built-in 3D viewer, and export to 10+ formats.\",\"Title\":\"Image to 3D Quality\"},\"Plugins\":{\"Competitor\":\"No plugins. Outputs GLB only — manual import into any DCC tool required.\",\"Meshy\":\"Native plugins for Blender, Unity, Unreal Engine, Maya, 3DS Max, Godot, and Roblox. One-click import/export.\"},\"Pricing\":{\"Competitor\":\"Free to download and use (MIT license). But you must supply your own Linux server with a 24GB+ NVIDIA GPU — the hidden cost is infrastructure.\",\"Meshy\":\"SaaS subscription — see meshy.ai/pricing for current plans. No infrastructure required — compute runs on Meshy's cloud. Free tier with 100 credits/month.\",\"Title\":\"Cost of Use\"},\"TextTo3D\":{\"Competitor\":\"Not supported. Trellis 2 is image-to-3D only. Microsoft recommends using a text-to-image pipeline to generate an image first, then feed it into Trellis 2.\",\"Meshy\":\"Natural language prompts with 500+ style presets — realistic, anime, cartoon, voxel, sculpture. Full textured model in under 60 seconds.\"}},\"Faq\":{\"API\":{\"A\":\"No. Trellis 2 has no hosted API. It runs locally via Python after downloading model weights from Hugging Face. A web demo is available on Hugging Face Spaces but is not suitable for production use. Meshy provides a full REST API with webhooks, batch processing, and versioned endpoints.\",\"Q\":\"Does Trellis 2 have a hosted API?\"},\"Animation\":{\"A\":\"No. Trellis 2 outputs static GLB meshes only — there is no rigging, no animation workflow, and no motion library. Meshy includes auto-rigging for humanoid and quadruped characters, a library of 500+ preset animations, and direct export to Unity and Unreal Engine.\",\"Q\":\"Does Trellis 2 support animation or rigging?\"},\"Commercial\":{\"A\":\"It's complicated. Trellis 2's core code is MIT-licensed, but its texturing pipeline depends on nvdiffrast — an NVIDIA library under the NVIDIA Source Code License, which requires separate authorization from NVIDIA for commercial use. Assets generated using Trellis 2's native PBR texturing cannot be sold commercially without that authorization. The community has been working on replacing these dependencies. Meshy paid plans include full commercial ownership with no such restrictions.\",\"Q\":\"Is Trellis 2 free to use commercially?\"},\"Formats\":{\"A\":\"Trellis 2 exports GLB format with PBR materials (Base Color, Roughness, Metallic, Opacity). It does not natively export FBX, OBJ, STL, USDZ, or 3MF. Meshy exports FBX, GLB, OBJ, STL, USDZ, 3MF, and BLEND.\",\"Q\":\"What file formats does Trellis 2 export?\"},\"FreePlan\":{\"Q\":\"Does Meshy offer a free plan?\"},\"GPU\":{\"A\":\"Yes — Trellis 2 requires a Linux machine with at least 24GB of NVIDIA GPU memory (tested on A100 and H100). It also requires CUDA 12.4, Python 3.8+, and Conda. Windows is not fully supported. Meshy runs entirely in the browser with no local hardware requirements.\",\"Q\":\"Do I need a GPU or special hardware to use Trellis 2?\"},\"GameDev\":{\"A\":\"Meshy is the significantly stronger choice for game developers. It offers 500+ preset animations, auto-rigging, full PBR textures, and native plugins for Unity, Unreal Engine, Godot, and Roblox. Trellis 2 outputs static GLB meshes with no animation, no rigging, and no engine integrations — requiring substantial additional work to integrate into a game pipeline.\",\"Q\":\"Which is better for game development?\"},\"Install\":{\"A\":\"Installing Trellis 2 requires a Linux machine with an NVIDIA GPU (≥24GB VRAM), CUDA 12.4, Python 3.8+, and Conda. The official steps are: clone the Microsoft Trellis 2 GitHub repository, create a Conda environment, install dependencies via pip (including spconv, xformers, and nvdiffrast), then run inference via the provided Python scripts or a Gradio demo. On a fresh Linux system, the setup typically takes 1–3 hours. Windows is not officially supported. Third-party one-click installers exist (e.g. for Windows via StableProjectorz) but are community-maintained and may have compatibility issues. If you want to skip installation entirely, Meshy generates the same type of 3D models directly in your browser — no downloads, no GPU, no configuration required.\",\"Q\":\"How do I install and use Trellis 2?\"},\"Learning\":{\"A\":\"For most users, Meshy is significantly easier. Meshy is browser-based — type a prompt or upload an image, click Generate, and download your result in under 60 seconds. Trellis 2 requires setting up a Linux environment, installing CUDA 12.4 and Conda, downloading model weights, and running Python scripts. There is no consumer web interface for Trellis 2 other than a limited Hugging Face Spaces demo.\",\"Q\":\"Is Meshy harder to learn than Trellis 2?\"},\"OS\":{\"A\":\"Trellis 2 officially supports Linux only. The repository notes Windows as 'not fully tested' and macOS is not mentioned at all. Setting it up requires CUDA 12.4, Conda, and a 24GB+ NVIDIA GPU — hardware that is only available in Linux server environments. Meshy runs entirely in the browser on Windows, Mac, Linux, iOS, and Android — no installation required.\",\"Q\":\"Can I use Trellis 2 on Windows or Mac?\"},\"Ownership\":{\"A\":\"On Meshy's paid plans, you own the outputs entirely — full commercial rights with no attribution required. On the free plan, assets are licensed under CC BY 4.0 (commercial use with attribution). Trellis 2's situation is more complex: the core model is MIT-licensed, but the texturing pipeline depends on nvdiffrast (NVIDIA Source Code License), which requires separate NVIDIA authorization before commercial distribution. If you plan to sell assets, Meshy's paid plan is the simpler, legally clearer option.\",\"Q\":\"Who owns the 3D models I generate with Meshy?\"},\"Printing\":{\"A\":\"Meshy is the better choice for 3D printing. Meshy generates optimized, watertight meshes and exports STL, 3MF, and OBJ with one-click Bambu Studio integration and a 97% slicer pass rate. Trellis 2 exports GLB only, with no print-specific tooling, no watertight mesh guarantees, and no slicer integrations.\",\"Q\":\"How does Trellis 2 compare for 3D printing?\"},\"Retexture\":{\"A\":\"No — Trellis 2 generates textures as part of its mesh output pipeline only. It cannot apply new textures to a mesh you already have. Meshy's AI Texturing engine generates full PBR maps on any mesh, including assets you didn't create in Meshy.\",\"Q\":\"Can Trellis 2 retexture an existing mesh?\"},\"TextTo3D\":{\"A\":\"No. Trellis 2 is image-to-3D only — there is no text input support. The Microsoft team explicitly notes this limitation and recommends routing through a text-to-image model first to generate a reference image. This adds friction and dependency on a second AI tool. Meshy supports both text-to-3D and image-to-3D natively in the same browser-based workflow.\",\"Q\":\"Does Trellis 2 support text-to-3D generation?\"},\"WhatIs\":{\"A\":\"Trellis 2 is an open-source image-to-3D generation model developed by Microsoft Research. It takes a single image as input and outputs a textured 3D mesh in GLB format, using a sparse structured latent representation to capture geometry and appearance. Trellis 2 is self-hosted — there is no cloud product or API. Running it requires a Linux machine with at least 24GB of NVIDIA GPU memory (VRAM), CUDA 12.4, and Python. It does not support text-to-3D input, rigging, animation, or retexturing existing assets. Meshy covers all of these in a browser-based platform with no installation required.\",\"Q\":\"What is Trellis 2?\"}},\"Feature\":{\"AITexturing\":\"AI Texturing\",\"AnimationRigging\":\"Animation \u0026 Rigging\",\"EnterpriseFeatures\":\"Enterprise Features\",\"ImageTo3D\":\"Image to 3D\",\"PluginEcosystem\":\"Plugin Ecosystem\",\"SetupRequired\":\"Setup Required\",\"StartingPrice\":\"Starting Price\",\"TextTo3D\":\"Text to 3D\"},\"Features\":{\"Animation\":{\"CTA\":\"Browse the Animation Library\",\"Description\":\"Meshy includes auto-rigging and a library of 500+ preset animations — walk cycles, attacks, idles, and more. Export rigged, animated characters directly to Unity, Unreal Engine, Godot, or Roblox in one click. Trellis 2 has no rigging or animation support — it outputs static GLB meshes only.\",\"Label\":\"Animation\",\"Title\":\"500+ Ready-to-Use Animations, Out of the Box\"},\"ImageTo3D\":{\"CTA\":\"Try Image to 3D\",\"Description\":\"Meshy converts single images or multi-view photos into fully textured, PBR-ready 3D models. Unlike Trellis 2, Meshy also supports retexturing existing assets — giving you full control over any mesh.\",\"Title\":\"Turn Any Photo Into a 3D Model\"},\"Printing\":{\"CTA\":\"See 3D Printing Workflow\",\"Description\":\"Meshy generates optimized, watertight meshes ready for slicing — no cleanup in Blender or Meshmixer needed. Export in STL, 3MF, or OBJ and send directly to Bambu Studio with one click. Trellis 2 only exports GLB format with no print-specific tooling or slicer integrations.\",\"Label\":\"3D Printing\",\"Title\":\"From Idea to Print-Ready in Minutes\"},\"TextTo3D\":{\"CTA\":\"Try Text to 3D\",\"Description\":\"Type a description, get a textured 3D model in under 60 seconds. Meshy supports 500+ art style presets across realistic, anime, cartoon, voxel, and sculpture. Trellis 2 is image-to-3D only — text input is not supported.\",\"Title\":\"From Prompt to Production-Ready 3D\"},\"Texturing\":{\"CTA\":\"Retexture a Mesh\",\"Description\":\"Meshy generates full PBR texture maps — Albedo, Normal, Roughness, Metallic, and AO — on any mesh, including models you didn't create in Meshy. Trellis 2's texturing is limited to its mesh output and doesn't support retexturing existing assets.\",\"Label\":\"Texturing\",\"Title\":\"AI Texture Generation on Any 3D Mesh\"}},\"Hero\":{\"Description\":\"Trying to decide between Meshy and Trellis 2? The right choice depends on whether you need a ready-to-use platform or a self-hosted research model. Explore why creators, game developers, and 3D printing enthusiasts choose Meshy over open-source alternatives.\",\"LastUpdated\":\"May 2026\",\"ReadTime\":\"7 min read\",\"TitleHighlight\":\"Which AI 3D Generator\",\"TitlePart1\":\"Meshy vs. Trellis 2:\",\"TitlePart3\":\"Should You Choose?\"},\"NA\":\"N/A\",\"None\":\"None\",\"NotApplicable\":\"Not applicable\",\"NotSupported\":\"Not supported\",\"RelatedComparisons\":{\"Hunyuan3D\":{\"Description\":\"Tencent's open-source 3D foundation model compared\",\"Title\":\"Meshy vs Hunyuan3D\"},\"Tripo\":{\"Description\":\"Compare two leading AI 3D generation platforms\",\"Title\":\"Meshy vs Tripo\"}},\"SpeedBenchmark\":{\"Note\":\"Trellis 2 generation time measured on RTX 3060 at 1024³ resolution via community benchmark (r/LocalLLM). Meshy runs on cloud infrastructure — no local GPU required.\",\"OSMeshy\":\"Any\",\"Setup\":\"Setup\",\"SetupCompetitor\":\"Hours\",\"SetupMeshy\":\"None\",\"Topology\":{\"CompetitorCap1\":\"Raw GLB output only\",\"CompetitorCap2\":\"No UV tools or texture pipeline\",\"CompetitorCap3\":\"No rigging or animation support\",\"CompetitorCap4\":\"All post-processing on you\",\"Factor1Competitor\":\"Required (~990K tris)\",\"Factor1Label\":\"Retopology required\",\"Factor1Meshy\":\"Optional\",\"Factor2Label\":\"Auto UV / texturing\",\"Factor3Label\":\"Auto rigging\",\"Factor4Label\":\"Low-poly mode\",\"Factor5Label\":\"Web workflow\",\"MeshyCap1\":\"Low Poly Mode — stable triangle output\",\"MeshyCap2\":\"Automatic UV mapping \u0026 PBR texturing\",\"MeshyCap3\":\"Auto-rigging \u0026 500+ preset animations\",\"MeshyCap4\":\"Browser-based — no external tools needed\",\"NoCompetitor\":\"No\",\"NoteLink\":\"r/StableDiffusion community testing\",\"NotePrefix\":\"Trellis 2 triangle count from\",\"NoteSuffix\":\"at 1024³ resolution. All post-generation processing (retopology, UV, rigging) must be done manually in external DCC tools.\",\"YesMeshy\":\"Yes\"}},\"Table\":{\"Animation\":{\"AutoRigging\":\"Auto-Rigging\",\"AutoRiggingMeshy\":\"Humanoid \u0026 quadruped\",\"Export\":\"Rigged Character Export\",\"ExportMeshy\":\"Animated FBX/GLB with full skeleton \u0026 weights\",\"Library\":\"Animation Library\",\"LibraryMeshy\":\"500+ presets (walk, run, idle, combat, dance, emotes)\",\"Title\":\"Animation \u0026 Motion\"},\"Generation\":{\"ArtStylesCompetitor\":\"No style control — output follows input image\",\"ArtStylesFeature\":\"Art Styles\",\"ArtStylesMeshy\":\"Realistic, Anime, Cartoon, Voxel, Sculpture\",\"ImageTo3DCompetitor\":\"Single image (primary strength)\",\"ImageTo3DFeature\":\"Image-to-3D\",\"ImageTo3DMeshy\":\"Single \u0026 multi-view\",\"LatestModelFeature\":\"Latest Model\",\"PlatformCompetitor\":\"Linux only (Windows not fully tested)\",\"PlatformFeature\":\"Platform Support\",\"PlatformMeshy\":\"All platforms via browser\",\"SetupCompetitor\":\"Linux, NVIDIA GPU ≥24GB VRAM, CUDA 12.4, Conda\",\"SetupMeshy\":\"None — fully browser-based\",\"TextTo3DFeature\":\"Text-to-3D\",\"TextTo3DMeshy\":\"Natural language \u0026 image prompts\",\"TimeCompetitor\":\"~20s–4 min on local GPU (requires 24GB+ VRAM)\",\"TimeFeature\":\"Generation Time\",\"TimeMeshy\":\"~1 min (cloud, no GPU required)\",\"Title\":\"3D Generation\"},\"Integrations\":{\"API\":\"Hosted API\",\"APICompetitor\":\"No hosted API — self-hosted Python inference only\",\"APIMeshy\":\"Full REST API with Playground \u0026 versioned endpoints\",\"CustomPipeline\":\"Custom Pipeline Integration\",\"CustomPipelineCompetitor\":\"Python library via Hugging Face (self-hosted)\",\"CustomPipelineMeshy\":\"REST API + webhooks + batch processing\",\"ExportFormats\":\"Export Formats\",\"ExportFormatsCompetitor\":\"GLB only\",\"Plugins\":\"Engine \u0026 DCC Plugins\",\"PluginsCompetitor\":\"None — manual GLB import only\",\"Printing\":\"3D Printing Integration\",\"PrintingCompetitor\":\"GLB export only; no slicer integration\",\"PrintingMeshy\":\"Native Bambu Studio one-click send; STL/3MF for any slicer\",\"Security\":\"Security Certifications\",\"SecurityCompetitor\":\"N/A — self-hosted open-source\",\"TeamMgmt\":\"Team \u0026 User Management\",\"TeamMgmtMeshy\":\"Team workspace, multi-user access, role-based permissions\",\"Title\":\"Integrations \u0026 Workflow\"},\"Pricing\":{\"AnnualDiscount\":\"Annual Discount\",\"AnnualDiscountMeshy\":\"Save 20%\",\"AssetRetention\":\"Asset Retention\",\"AssetRetentionCompetitor\":\"Local storage — you control your own files\",\"AssetRetentionMeshy\":\"3 days (Pro/Studio) / Forever (Enterprise)\",\"CommercialLicense\":\"Commercial License\",\"CommercialLicenseCompetitor\":\"MIT core, but texturing pipeline depends on nvdiffrast (NVIDIA Source License) — commercial use requires separate NVIDIA authorization\",\"CommercialLicenseMeshy\":\"Full ownership on paid; CC BY 4.0 on free\",\"CostModel\":\"Cost Model\",\"CostModelCompetitor\":\"Free model weights, but requires your own 24GB+ GPU server\",\"CostModelMeshy\":\"SaaS subscription — no infrastructure needed\",\"EntryPlan\":\"Entry Paid Plan\",\"EntryPlanCompetitor\":\"N/A — no paid tier\",\"EntryPlanMeshy\":\"Pro plan — see meshy.ai/pricing\",\"FreeAccess\":\"Free Access\",\"FreeAccessCompetitor\":\"Fully free — MIT licensed, self-hosted\",\"FreeAccessMeshy\":\"100 monthly credits (no credit card)\",\"Title\":\"Pricing \u0026 Access\"},\"Quality\":{\"AITexturingCompetitor\":\"Textures generated as part of mesh output only; no standalone retexturing\",\"AITexturingMeshy\":\"Dedicated AI Texturing engine — retexture any mesh\",\"AITexturingStandalone\":\"AI Texturing (standalone)\",\"ComplexTopology\":\"Complex Topology\",\"ComplexTopologyCompetitor\":\"Handles open surfaces, non-manifold geometry, and internal structures\",\"ComplexTopologyMeshy\":\"Optimized for production-ready meshes\",\"MeshTopology\":\"Mesh Topology\",\"MeshTopologyCompetitor\":\"Sparse voxel-based representation; handles complex and non-manifold geometry\",\"MeshTopologyMeshy\":\"Clean meshes with good edge flow\",\"OutputResolution\":\"Output Resolution\",\"OutputResolutionCompetitor\":\"Up to 1536³ voxel resolution on H100\",\"OutputResolutionMeshy\":\"High-quality textured meshes\",\"PBRSupport\":\"PBR Material Support\",\"PBRSupportCompetitor\":\"Base Color texture only; Roughness and Metallic are fixed constants with no separate maps\",\"PBRSupportMeshy\":\"Full PBR (Albedo, Normal, Metallic, Roughness, AO)\",\"PrintReadiness\":\"3D Print-Readiness\",\"PrintReadinessCompetitor\":\"GLB export only; no print-specific tooling\",\"PrintReadinessMeshy\":\"97% slicer pass rate; Bambu Studio integration; 3MF export\",\"Title\":\"Output Quality\"},\"Ratings\":{\"Community\":\"Community Size\",\"CommunityCompetitor\":\"GitHub research project\",\"CommunityMeshy\":\"10M+ users worldwide\",\"Enterprise\":\"Enterprise Readiness\",\"EnterpriseCompetitor\":\"No enterprise support or certifications\",\"EnterpriseMeshy\":\"SOC 2 + ISO 27001 certified, dedicated support\",\"G2\":\"G2 Rating\",\"G2Competitor\":\"Not listed — open-source research model\",\"Support\":\"Customer Support\",\"SupportCompetitor\":\"GitHub Issues only\",\"SupportMeshy\":\"Email + Help Center + dedicated Enterprise support\",\"Title\":\"Ratings \u0026 Trust\",\"Trustpilot\":\"Trustpilot Rating\",\"TrustpilotCompetitor\":\"Not listed\"}},\"Tldr\":{\"CompetitorPitch\":\"You're an ML researcher or engineer who needs free, open-source model weights for a custom self-hosted pipeline and has access to a 24GB GPU server.\",\"CompetitorSummary\":\"is Microsoft's open-source image-to-3D model — self-hosted, no cloud API, requires a Linux server with a 24GB NVIDIA GPU. It's the better pick if you're a researcher or ML engineer who needs free model weights for a custom pipeline, and can accept that commercial distribution requires separate NVIDIA authorization.\",\"MeshyPitch\":\"You need a complete 3D pipeline today: generation, texturing, rigging, animation, and engine integrations, with no Linux server or GPU required.\",\"MeshySummary\":\"is a full production platform: generate from text or image, texture with PBR maps, auto-rig, animate with 500+ presets, and export to every major engine or slicer. With 7 native plugins, enterprise-grade security, and 10M+ users, it works entirely in your browser with no GPU or installation required.\"},\"WhoShouldChoose\":{\"Competitor\":{\"GPU\":\"You have access to a Linux server with a 24GB+ NVIDIA GPU and prefer full control over your infrastructure\",\"ML\":\"You're an ML researcher or engineer who needs an open-source model to integrate into a custom self-hosted pipeline\",\"NonManifold\":\"Your use case involves complex or non-manifold geometry that benefits from Trellis 2's sparse voxel representation\",\"Resolution\":\"You need the highest possible output resolution — Trellis 2 supports up to 1536³ voxels on H100-class hardware\",\"Weights\":\"You need open model weights for research or internal use — Trellis 2's core is MIT-licensed, though commercial deployment requires separate nvdiffrast authorization\"},\"Meshy\":{\"API\":\"A hosted API is required — Meshy provides a full REST API with webhooks and batch processing; Trellis 2 requires self-hosted Python inference\",\"Animation\":\"Animation matters — Meshy includes auto-rigging and 500+ preset animations; Trellis 2 outputs static meshes with no animation support\",\"GPU\":\"You don't have a Linux server or 24GB GPU — Meshy runs entirely in the browser, no installation or hardware required\",\"Platform\":\"You want a production-ready platform — trusted by 10M+ users worldwide, rated {rating}/5 on G2 across {count} reviews\",\"Plugins\":\"You need engine integrations — Meshy has native plugins for Blender, Unity, Unreal Engine, Maya, 3DS Max, Godot, and Roblox; Trellis 2 has none\",\"TextTo3D\":\"Text-to-3D is part of your workflow — Meshy supports natural language prompts; Trellis 2 is image-only with no text input\"}}},\"VsTripo\":{\"RelatedComparisons\":{\"Hunyuan3D\":{\"Description\":\"Tencent's open-source 3D foundation model compared\",\"Title\":\"Meshy vs Hunyuan3D\"}}},\"WhyMeshyBetter\":{\"Description\":\"See what {count} users worldwide say across independent review platforms.\",\"G2Rating\":\"G2 Rating: 4.8\",\"G2Reviews\":\"{count} reviews\",\"ProductHuntFollowers\":\"{count} followers\",\"ProductHuntRating\":\"Product Hunt Rating: 4.8\",\"Title\":\"Trusted by Creators Worldwide\",\"TrustpilotRating\":\"Trustpilot Rating: 4.8\",\"TrustpilotReviews\":\"{count} reviews\"}},\"LotteryPopup\":{\"AppliedBanner\":\"🎁 Welcome Gift: {percent}% OFF unlocked\",\"Close\":\"Close\",\"PlanName\":{\"ProMonthly\":\"Pro Monthly\",\"ProQuarterly\":\"Pro Quarterly\",\"ProYearly\":\"Pro Yearly\"},\"PrimaryButton\":{\"BuyOneGetN\":\"Get {plan} — Buy 1 Month, Get {n} Free\",\"ProMonthly\":\"Claim {percent}% OFF Pro Monthly\",\"ProQuarterly\":\"Claim {percent}% OFF Pro Quarterly\",\"ProYearly\":\"Claim {percent}% OFF Pro Yearly\"},\"WonAndClaim\":\"🎉 You unwrapped a Welcome Gift: {percent}% OFF!\"},\"PrintIssueReport\":{\"Add\":\"Add\",\"AttachPhotos\":\"Attach photos (optional, up to {max})\",\"Cancel\":\"Cancel\",\"EmptyModels\":\"No downloaded models yet\",\"Entry\":\"Report a print issue\",\"ErrorToast\":\"Failed to submit feedback, please try again.\",\"LoadingModels\":\"Loading…\",\"Placeholder\":\"e.g. supports wouldn't come off, walls too thin, size was off, texture didn't print…\",\"ProcessLabel\":\"What are you printing with? (optional)\",\"ProcessMultiFdm\":\"Multi-color FDM\",\"ProcessResin\":\"Resin\",\"ProcessSingleFdm\":\"Single-color FDM\",\"SelectModel\":\"Which model had the issue?\",\"Submit\":\"Submit\",\"Subtitle\":\"Something went wrong with a print — or stopped you before you could print? Let us know. Your report goes straight to our team.\",\"SuccessToast\":\"Feedback submitted, thank you!\",\"Title\":\"Report a Print Issue\",\"UntitledModel\":\"Untitled model\",\"WhatHappened\":\"What happened?\"},\"RetentionOfferModal\":{\"Body\":\"We'd hate to see you go — so we've added a free month of Pro to your account. It's already yours. Stay with us one more month; we think you'll love what's coming.\",\"Cta\":\"Alright, one more month!\",\"Title\":\"We don't want to say goodbye 🥺\"},\"ShowcaseDialog\":{\"Close\":\"Close\"},\"SimReady\":{\"Cancel\":\"Cancel\",\"Close\":\"Close\",\"Submit\":\"Send to OV/Isaac\",\"Title\":\"Sim-Ready Properties\",\"WindowsOnly\":\"OV/Isaac bridge is only available on Windows\"},\"WaitTimeTips\":{\"Batch\":\"Generate a batch, compare, then choose your favorite\",\"BatchDetail\":\"Drop in multiple images and Batch Images to 3D starts every task together. Perfect when you have a whole set of ideas ready to turn into 3D.\",\"CleanImage\":\"Clear, centered subjects on plain backgrounds give sharper results\",\"CleanImageDetail\":\"For Image to 3D, the cleaner the photo, the better the model. Use a single subject centered on a plain background, and avoid busy scenes, since Meshy works best with one object at a time.\",\"ExploreOnMyOwn\":\"Explore on my own\",\"ImageWorkspace\":\"Refine the look in Image Workspace before going 3D\",\"ImageWorkspaceDetail\":\"Your 3D model is only as good as the image behind it. Pop into Image Workspace to create or edit images, adjust the outfit or pose, and tidy up the background before you hit generate in 3D.\",\"Pro\":\"Go Pro to run up to 10 tasks in parallel\",\"ProDetail\":\"Pro lets you generate up to 10 models in parallel, so you don't have to wait on one before starting the next. Queue your next task now.\",\"Retexture\":\"Reskin a model with AI Texturing\",\"RetextureDetail\":\"Apply AI Texturing to an existing model to instantly swap color schemes or material styles, with no re-modeling needed. One model, many variations.\",\"Retry\":\"Results vary, so try a few and keep the best\",\"RetryDetail\":\"AI generation is a little unpredictable, so every run comes out slightly different. If the first model isn't quite right, generate again.\",\"SectionTitle\":\"Tips \u0026 Tricks\",\"TipLabel\":\"Tip\",\"TryItNow\":\"Try it now\"}},\"Copilot\":{\"CoachMark\":{\"CreateImage\":{\"Description\":\"Edit Images in Meshy Helper by Simply Asking\"}},\"CreateImage\":\"Create Image\",\"CreateImageActiveTip\":\"Click to exit this mode\",\"CreateImageDisabledTip\":\"Only prompts for image generation can be created here.\",\"CreateImageInactiveTip\":\"Click to enter this mode\",\"CreateImageTip\":\"Limited-time Free\",\"CreateImageTips\":\"Click to enter this mode\",\"NewChat\":\"New Chat\",\"Untitled\":\"Untitled\"},\"CreativeLab\":{\"StartDesignGate\":{\"ExhaustedTooltip\":\"Subscribe and Unlock unlimited attempt\",\"FreeDesignTooltip\":\"{tier} tier includes {limit} free designs per day — {remaining} left today.\",\"WarningBadge\":\"{remaining}/{limit} today\"}},\"CreditsUsagePaywall\":{\"Balance\":{\"ExpireNote\":\"\u003cstrong\u003e{amount} credits\u003c/strong\u003e expire {date}\",\"Heading\":\"Credits Balance\",\"Unit\":\"credits\",\"UpcomingExpiry\":{\"ExpiresOn\":\"expire on {date}\",\"Heading\":\"Credits expiration\"}},\"Card\":{\"MonthlyCredits\":\"monthly credits\",\"MultiplierComparison\":\"{multiplier} more than {current}\",\"MultiplierTag\":\"{multiplier} {tier}\",\"UpgradeFromBadge\":\"Upgrade from {current}\"},\"Cycle\":{\"MonthlyLabel\":\"Pay Monthly\",\"SaveLabel\":\"{percent} OFF\",\"YearlyLabel\":\"Pay Yearly\"},\"Dialog\":{\"A11yDescription\":\"View your credits usage history and upgrade your plan.\",\"Title\":\"Credits\"},\"Diff\":{\"ConcurrentTasks\":\"concurrent tasks\",\"CreditsPerMonth\":\"credits / mo\",\"CreditsResetTooltip\":\"Plan credits reset monthly and do not accumulate.\",\"FreeRetries\":\"free retries / task\",\"PriorityQueue\":\"priority queue\"},\"Enterprise\":{\"Action\":\"Contact sales\",\"Benefits\":{\"ApiRetention\":\"Forever API asset retention\",\"Concurrent\":\"50+ concurrent tasks\",\"Credits\":\"Customizable credit balance\",\"DataRetention\":\"Configurable data retention\",\"EverythingInStudio\":\"Everything in Studio, plus:\",\"FullApi\":\"Full API access\",\"Priority\":\"Highest queue priority\",\"Retries\":\"Unlimited free retries\",\"SamlSso\":\"SAML SSO\",\"Speed\":\"60% faster generation speed\",\"Support\":\"Dedicated account support\",\"TeamManagement\":\"Multiple team / workspace management\"},\"Current\":\"Current plan\",\"PrivilegesHeading\":\"Enterprise privileges\",\"Subtitle\":\"Volume credits, dedicated support, and custom terms.\",\"Tag\":\"Enterprise\",\"Title\":\"Need more? Talk to our team\"},\"ExtraCredits\":{\"BuyButton\":\"Buy\",\"SubscriberOnly\":\"Subscriber only\",\"Subtitle\":\"Top up just what you need without changing your plan.\",\"Title\":\"Or purchase extra credits\"},\"Footer\":{\"BuyCredits\":\"Buy credits\"},\"History\":{\"A11y\":{\"FirstPage\":\"First page\",\"LastPage\":\"Last page\",\"NextPage\":\"Next page\",\"PreviousPage\":\"Previous page\"},\"Column\":{\"Date\":\"Date\",\"DateTime\":\"Date\",\"Remaining\":\"Remaining\",\"Spent\":\"Spent\",\"Time\":\"Time\"},\"Heading\":\"Recent credits usage\",\"JumpToPage\":\"Go to\",\"PageOfTotal\":\"of {total}\",\"Range\":\"{start}-{end} of {total}\",\"WindowTooltip\":\"Showing credits usage from the last 90 days.\"},\"Price\":{\"BilledMonthly\":\"Billed monthly\",\"BilledYearly\":\"Billed yearly · {price}\",\"Next